你了解排灯节吗？

154
00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.510
I did, but I grew up overseas, you know?
我了解，但我是在海外长大的，你知道吧？

155
00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.610
I grew up in Indonesia.
我在印度尼西亚长大。

156
00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.190
Bali has a very big Hindu population.
巴厘岛有非常庞大的印度教人口。

157
00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:59.470
So I had heard of Diwali, and I thought it was awesome that we were going to do an episode
所以我听说过排灯节，而且我觉得我们要拍一集关于它的内容，

158
00:06:59.470 --> 00:06:59.970
about it.
这太棒了。

159
00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.810
Had you ever celebrated Diwali?
你以前庆祝过排灯节吗？

160
00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:05.610
I hadn't ever celebrated it, but myself, I went to an international school.
我以前从未庆祝过，但我自己上的是国际学校。

161
00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:10.690
They did recognize, you know, many holidays, and there was like a Diwali day.
他们确实会庆祝很多节日，而且还有类似排灯节这样的日子。

162
00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.650
Yeah, well, they do that at my kid's school now.
是啊，我孩子现在的学校也会这样做。

163
00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:18.350
They have a day where they celebrate Diwali, which I think is really cool, especially since
他们有一天会庆祝排灯节，我觉得这真的很酷，尤其是因为

164
00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:19.790
I grew up not knowing about it.
我小时候根本不知道这个节日。

165
00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:21.810
It is so beautiful, and it was so fun.
它太美了，而且非常有趣。

166
00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.510
I remember we were all really giddy.
我记得我们当时都特别兴奋。

167
00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.670
Of course, this meant we got to leave the office.
当然，这意味着我们可以离开办公室了。

168
00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.390
That brings me to fast fact number two, Angela.
这让我想到了第二个速查事实，安吉拉。

169
00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:30.490
Fan question from Juliet G.
来自朱丽叶·G.

170
00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:31.690
and Phoebe Tomac.
和菲比·托马克的粉丝提问。

171
00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.850
Where did you shoot the scenes when you were celebrating Diwali?
你们拍摄排灯节庆祝场景的地方是在哪儿？

172
00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.490
Well, guess who I went to for the answer?
嗯，猜猜我去找谁问的答案？

173
00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:40.450
Does it rhyme with Schmentish Media?
是不是押韵“肯特媒体”？

174
00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.710
It does, and we have a sting for it.
没错，我们还专门为它做了一个过场音效。

175
00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:43.250
You do?
真的吗？

176
00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:55.020
Yes, Angela, that was sent in by Tyler Beckwith, and we love it, Tyler.
是的，安吉拉，那是泰勒·贝克威斯发给我们的，我们很喜欢，泰勒。

177
00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.860
Thank you for our Kentopedia sting.
谢谢你为我们制作了“肯特百科”的过场音效。

178
00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.660
It is really great.
它真的很棒。

179
00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:01.280
It sounds like something out of like a 1980s action kind of movie.
听起来就像是那种20世纪80年代动作电影里的配乐。

180
00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:02.540
Exactly.
完全正确。

181
00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:09.000
Well, Kentopedia told us that Diwali was shot at Grant High School.
嗯，“肯特百科”告诉我们，排灯节是在格兰特高中拍摄的。

182
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:15.220
We shot most of the scenes in their gym, which is called Grant Hall, and we shot there at the end
我们大部分场景是在他们的体育馆拍摄的，那里叫格兰特大厅，我们是在八月底在那里拍摄的，

183
00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.700
of August, and school was in session.
当时学校已经开学了。

184
00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.080
They had just started up the school year.
他们刚开始新学年。

185
00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:26.860
He said that we shot there for three full days, and we had to work around the school schedule
他说我们在那里拍了整整三天，而且必须配合学校的时间表，

186
00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:30.400
because, like, school was happening in the hallways.
因为走廊里还有学生在上课。

187
00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:37.220
I have such a fond memory of our time shooting there because they parked our trailers facing sort
我对在那里拍摄的那段时光有着非常美好的回忆，因为他们把我们的拖车停在了一片

188
00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:44.320
of like a little field with some trees, and normally they were just in an asphalt parking lot.
有树的小草地对面，而平时我们通常都停在沥青停车场里。

189
00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:50.120
And so I would open my door, and there'd be trees and grass, and Brian brought a football,
所以我一打开门，就能看到树木和草地，布莱恩带了一个橄榄球，

190
00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:55.200
and we, like, tossed the football out in the grass, and I have such fond memories of this whole week.
我们在草地上抛接橄榄球，我对那一整周都有着非常美好的回忆。

191
00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.000
I remember it, too, for those exact same reasons.
我也记得，原因和你的一模一样。

192
00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:05.600
Well, this school is host to a lot of filmmaking, including Freaks and Geeks, Black-ish, Malcolm in the Middle,
嗯，这所学校是很多影视作品的取景地，包括《怪胎与书呆》、《黑人一家亲》、《马尔柯姆的一家》

193
00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:08.680
and True Blood, and I've got a little bit of trivia for you.
和《真爱如血》，我这里还有个小知识要告诉你。

194
00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:09.420
Yeah?
是吗？

195
00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.920
Melora Harden went to Grant High School.
梅洛拉·哈登就是格兰特高中毕业的。

196
00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:12.840
Get out of town.
别开玩笑了。

197
00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.100
Yeah, we shot at her alma mater.
没错，我们在她的母校拍摄的。

198
00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:15.780
Wow.
哇。

199
00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.360
I love that.
我喜欢这个巧合。

200
00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.500
She's, like, a true sort of, like, Hollywood kid, you know?
她就像是个地道的“好莱坞孩子”，你懂吧？

201
00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:23.540
Like, there's all these things from her life, like, right here.
就像，她生活中的所有这些东西，都在这儿。

202
00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:28.380
To me, it's still all sort of, like, I still feel like a transplant in some ways in Los Angeles.
对我来说，在某些方面，我感觉自己就像是洛杉矶的移植体。

203
00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:34.680
Like, still to this day, if I'm ever out and about and I see the Hollywood sign, I'm like,
直到今天，如果我出门在外看到好莱坞标志，我还是会想，

204
00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.680
there's a Hollywood sign.
那是好莱坞标志。

205
00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:37.200
Oh, my God, it's a Hollywood sign.
天哪，那是好莱坞标志。

206
00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:42.500
But if I drive by and I see, like, a film crew filming something on the street,
但如果我开车经过，看到街上有剧组在拍戏，

207
00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:47.200
I get as excited as if they pulled up in my neighborhood in St. Louis as a kid.
我还是会像小时候在圣路易斯看到剧组开进我家附近一样兴奋。

208
00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.460
I'm like, ooh, what are they filming?
我会想，噢，他们在拍什么？

209
00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.260
Oh, look, I wonder what it is.
噢，快看，不知道那是什么。

210
00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.180
I wonder if we can find out who's the star.
不知道能不能看出谁是主演。

211
00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:52.940
Yeah, I look.
是啊，我会看。

212
00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.900
Like, I get that same reaction still.
我还是会有那种反应。

213
00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:55.220
Yeah, me too.
我也是。

214
00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.740
I drive by and I try to see, like, is there someone famous out there?
我开车经过时也会想，外面有没有什么名人？

215
00:09:58.700 --> 00:09:59.180
Exactly.
没错。

216
00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:01.020
So true.
太对了。

217
00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:05.520
Well, I'm going to move us along, Angela, because I know we want to get to our interview with Mindy.
好了，我们要继续了，安吉拉，因为我知道我们想开始对敏迪的采访了。

218
00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.200
Fast fact number three, I said earlier this was directed by Miguel Arteta.
第三个小知识，我之前说过这一集是由米格尔·阿特塔执导的。

219
00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:14.320
Angela, I was such a huge fan of Miguel.
安吉拉，我是米格尔的超级粉丝。

220
00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:19.560
When I found out he was going to direct this episode, this is the only episode he directed,
当我发现他要执导这一集时——这是他执导的唯一一集——

221
00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.260
I completely geeked out.
我简直兴奋坏了。

222
00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:25.400
So, okay, he had directed this little—
所以，好吧，他执导过那部小小的——

223
00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:25.960
Did you go up to him?
你有去找他吗？

224
00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:26.820
Were you dorky?
你表现得傻乎乎的吗？

225
00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:27.380
What'd you do?
你做了什么？

226
00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.020
Oh, Angela, I followed him around the entire week.
噢，安吉拉，我那一整周都跟着他。

227
00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:31.600
We bonded.
我们建立了感情。

228
00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:36.260
At the end of this week, I thought we were best friends and would work together forever on every future project.
那一周结束时，我以为我们成了最好的朋友，以后每个项目都要一起合作。

229
00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:45.060
And I'm not going to lie, every time there was, like, a script that I was sent or when I was trying to produce a movie myself,
我不骗你，每次我收到剧本，或者我自己尝试制作电影时，

230
00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:52.220
he was the first person I would go to because I was like, I'm literally, like, this guy is a genius.
他都是我第一个想到的人，因为我觉得，说真的，这家伙是个天才。

231
00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.100
I love him.
我爱死他了。

232
00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.100
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

233
00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.440
I didn't know you were, like, following him around everywhere.
我不知道你竟然到处跟着他。

234
00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:58.500
Oh, yeah.
噢，是的。

235
00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:01.020
I wanted everything about him to rub off on me.
我想让他身上的一切都感染我。

236
00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:10.800
So he had directed this little indie movie called Chuck and Buck, written by and starring Mike White, who, by the way, I also have stalked.
他执导过一部叫《查克和巴克》的小成本独立电影，由迈克·怀特编剧并主演，顺便说一句，我也跟踪过他。

237
00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.380
Yeah, I know that you stalked him.
是啊，我知道你跟踪过他。

238
00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:21.280
I got to work with him, and then that made me feel one step closer to Mike White, who I eventually managed to stalk and become—
我有机会和他合作，这让我感觉离迈克·怀特又近了一步，我最终成功跟踪了他并成为了——

239
00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:26.980
I became friends with Mike White, and then I eventually got to be in a Mike White movie starring Ben Stiller.
我和迈克·怀特成了朋友，后来我终于有机会出演了一部由本·斯蒂勒主演的迈克·怀特电影。

240
00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:36.020
And then after that happened, I was like, well, I can now retire because I have worked with my idol.
那件事之后，我就想，好吧，我可以退休了，因为我已经和我的偶像合作过了。

241
00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.420
I wrote in my journal about this week—
我在日记里写了那一周的事——

242
00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:39.640
Do you want to hear what I wrote, lady?
你想听听我写了什么吗，女士？

243
00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:40.960
Of course.
当然想。

244
00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.600
I always want to hear about your journal.
我一直都想听听你的日记。

245
00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.240
Your journal delights me.
你的日记让我很开心。

246
00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:46.640
It does.
确实如此。

247
00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.500
That's going to be your autobiography.
那以后会成为你的自传。

248
00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.020
A journal delights me by Jenna Fisher.
《日记让我开心》，作者：珍娜·费舍。

249
00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.480
I wrote that, and I wrote this.
我写了那个，还写了这个。

250
00:11:53.480 --> 00:12:01.000
Me and the adorable Mindy Kaling are going to be doing really early morning interviews together on all the local NBC stations.
我和可爱的敏迪·卡灵要一起在当地所有的NBC电视台进行非常早的晨间采访。

251
00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:07.120
We are going to talk to 16 cities, and we have to get up at 5 a.m.
我们要去连线16个城市，而且得在凌晨5点起床。

252
00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.240
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

253
00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.160
You guys did a little press junket.
你们当时做过一个小型的媒体见面会。

254
00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.180
I think this is my very first one.
我觉得那是我第一次参加。

255
00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:16.520
Well, what's crazy about that, Angela, is you probably then, after you were done, had to come to work.
安吉拉，最疯狂的是，你做完这些之后可能还得赶去上班。

256
00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:20.560
Oh, yeah, because we had to—I remember we had to be on stage.
噢，是的，因为我们必须——我记得我们得去片场。

257
00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:29.980
We actually did them on the set with the set as the background, and we got there, and we met this satellite media tour, is what they called it, and we met their crew.
我们实际上是在片场做的，以片场为背景，我们到了那里，见到了所谓的卫星媒体巡回采访组，还有他们的工作人员。

258
00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.740
And we had to be there at 4 a.m.
我们必须在凌晨4点赶到那里。

259
00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:41.080
to go through hair and makeup, and then we started doing interviews at 5 a.m., and we talked to a new city every 15 minutes for three hours.
去做妆发，然后从凌晨5点开始接受采访，每15分钟连线一个新城市，持续三个小时。

260
00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:41.600
Wow.
哇。

261
00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:41.860
Yeah.
是啊。

262
00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.840
And you did it with Mindy.
而且你是和敏迪一起做的。

263
00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.800
Mindy was my first press junket.
敏迪是我第一次媒体见面会的搭档。

264
00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:49.420
Well, this is a wonderful segue into our upcoming segment.
好了，这正好引出了我们接下来的环节。

265
00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:53.740
We'll take a break, but when we come back, we're going to play our interview with Mindy Kaling.
我们要休息一下，但回来之后，我们将播放对敏迪·卡灵的采访。

266
00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:55.100
She came and talked to us.
她来和我们聊了聊。

267
00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:55.780
It was amazing.
太棒了。

268
00:12:56.060 --> 00:13:01.760
It was such a joy to have her here, and I'm so excited for you guys to listen to this.
能请她来真是太高兴了，我很期待你们听到这段采访。

269
00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.700
And then afterwards, we're going to fully break down the episode.
之后，我们将深入剖析这一集。

270
00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.400
We'll get to that right after the break.
广告回来后我们就讲。

271
00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:07.480
We'll see you with Mindy.
稍后见，和敏迪一起。

272
00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:19.650
Hi.
嗨。

273
00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:21.070
Hi, guys.
嗨，伙计们。

274
00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:21.630
Hi.
嗨。

275
00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:22.990
I'm so happy to be here.
我很高兴能来到这里。

276
00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:27.870
Thank you.
谢谢。

277
00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.290
Congrats, you guys, on the massive success of this.
恭喜你们，节目取得了巨大的成功。

278
00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.570
This is awesome.
这太棒了。

279
00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:37.990
Everyone in my life is obviously such a fan, and I'm so proud of you guys.
我生活中的每个人显然都是你们的粉丝，我为你们感到骄傲。

280
00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:38.730
This is so great.
这真是太好了。

281
00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:39.670
Thank you.
谢谢。

282
00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:40.790
Thanks, Mindy.
谢谢你，敏迪。

283
00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:41.590
Yeah, of course.
不客气。

284
00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:42.290
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

285
00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:43.430
We're having a good time.
我们玩得很开心。

286
00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:52.910
It's fun to hear the way that the show was through your guys' eyes because it's so loving and fun and super accurate, and I'm really enjoying it.
听你们用自己的视角讲述这部剧很有趣，因为你们的视角充满了爱、乐趣，而且超级准确，我真的很享受。

287
00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:54.350
So this is great.
所以这真的很棒。

288
00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:55.210
Thanks for having me.
谢谢你们邀请我。

289
00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:56.250
Thank you.
谢谢。

290
00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.550
That was so nice.
太贴心了。

291
00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.710
I feel like this is all just pure joy.
我觉得这一切简直就是纯粹的快乐。

292
00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:04.990
I'm just so delighted to see you and to talk to you, and this is such a fun episode.
见到你们并和你们聊天我感到非常高兴，这一集真的很有趣。

293
00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.870
So we just get to reminisce a little bit.
所以我们正好可以借此机会回忆一下。

294
00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:07.470
Love it.
太喜欢了。

295
00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:13.370
Well, before we get into Diwali, we always like to ask all of our guests their office origin story.
那么，在进入“排灯节”那一集之前，我们总是喜欢问所有嘉宾他们的《办公室》起源故事。

296
00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:16.490
So how did you come to be on the show?
你是怎么加入这部剧的呢？

297
00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:29.810
Well, it was 2004, and I was doing a play off-off-Broadway in New York called Matt and Ben, which was a play that I wrote with my writing partner and friend at the time,
那是2004年，我当时在纽约演一部外外百老汇的剧，叫《马特与本》，那是我和当时的写作搭档兼好友一起写的剧本，

298
00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:30.450
Brenda Withers.
布伦达·威瑟斯。

299
00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:37.230
It's like an hour-long short play where I play Ben Affleck and she plays Matt Damon.
那是一部时长一小时的短剧，我演本·阿弗莱克，她演马特·达蒙。

300
00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:43.390
It's so hard to tell this story without being like, just being like, okay, so just ignore that kind of interesting fact and then move on.
讲这个故事真的很难，因为我总想说，好吧，忽略掉那个有趣的背景事实，然后继续往下讲。

301
00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:44.910
But so we did that.
但我们确实那样做了。

302
00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:49.530
It won the Fringe Festival, got some attention, and sort of was our entree to L.A.
它赢得了边缘艺术节的奖项，引起了一些关注，也算是我们进入洛杉矶的敲门砖。

303
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:55.250
And when we were in L.A., I had like an Arrested Development spec and then that play.
当我们到洛杉矶时，我手里有像《发展受阻》的样片剧本，还有那部戏。

304
00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:57.630
And I had very few meetings.
但我得到的面试机会非常少。

305
00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:06.470
The climate for hiring writers, if you were like an untested Indian-American woman, it was very different 16 years ago than it is now.
十六年前，如果你是一个未经考验的印度裔美国女性，编剧招聘的环境和现在大不相同。

306
00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:11.710
And the only place that I got an interview at, I got two interviews.
我唯一得到面试机会的地方，其实我拿到了两次面试。

307
00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:16.330
One was at Nevermind Nirvana, which was a pilot about an Indian family.
一个是《Nevermind Nirvana》，那是一部关于印度家庭的试播集。

308
00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:19.530
And I was like, yes, I can, yes, I could write on that show.
当时我想，太好了，我可以，我能为那部剧写剧本。

309
00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.070
And the other one was The Office.
另一个是《办公室》。

310
00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:28.050
And I remember Joey was like, do you guys remember how huge Joey was when we started shooting?
我记得当时《乔伊》很火，你们还记得我们刚开始拍摄时《乔伊》有多火吗？

311
00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:28.670
Yeah.
记得。

312
00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:29.090
Oh, yeah.
哦，记得。

313
00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.710
The Friends spinoff.
就是那部《老友记》的衍生剧。

314
00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:33.450
It was like the NBC, they put all their money in that.
当时NBC把所有的钱都投在了那部剧上。

315
00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:34.550
And then Father of the Pride.
还有《傲慢的父亲》。

316
00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.670
Do you guys remember that one?
你们还记得那部剧吗？

317
00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:36.430
No.
不记得。

318
00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:42.230
Father of the Pride was a cartoon, a Jeffrey Katzenberg-produced cartoon about,
《傲慢的父亲》是一部动画片，由杰弗瑞·卡森伯格制作，讲述的是……

319
00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:47.350
from the point of view of two tigers that worked with Siegfried and Roy.
从两只在齐格弗里德与罗伊手下工作的老虎的视角展开。

320
00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:48.190
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

321
00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:48.690
What?
什么？

322
00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:50.270
Yes, it's coming back to me.
没错，我想起来了。

323
00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.310
And it was an animated show.
那确实是一部动画片。

324
00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.950
This sounds like a bit on Saturday Night Live.
这听起来像是《周六夜现场》里的一个段子。

325
00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:55.850
This doesn't sound like a TV show.
这听起来不像是一部正经电视剧。

326
00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:58.870
Not only was it a real show, it was like the hottest show.
它不仅是一部真实的剧，而且当时还是最热门的剧。

327
00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.210
Like you could not get an interview.
你根本拿不到面试机会。

328
00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.170
So I didn't get an interview on Will and Grace.
所以我没能拿到《威尔和格蕾丝》的面试。

329
00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:05.070
I didn't get an interview at Joey.
也没能拿到《乔伊》的面试。

330
00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.830
And I didn't get an interview at Father of the Pride.
也没能拿到《傲慢的父亲》的面试。

331
00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.930
And you can imagine like just to show how things have become so different from them.
你可以想象一下，这足以说明现在的情况和当时有多么不同。

332
00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:16.310
Like, can you imagine like now, like a minority woman who won the Fringe Festival
试想一下现在，如果一个赢得了边缘艺术节奖项的少数族裔女性

333
00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:20.770
coming out to LA, not getting a meeting on like, on all the two shows.
来到洛杉矶，却连那两部剧的面试都拿不到。

334
00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:21.850
So things have changed a lot.
所以情况确实改变了很多。

335
00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:22.510
So that's great.
这很好。

336
00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:25.750
But the two people who I got interviews with Nevermind Nirvana,
但我唯一得到面试机会的那两部剧，其中之一是《Nevermind Nirvana》，

337
00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:28.150
and I went into their offices in Burbank.
我去了他们在伯班克的办公室。

338
00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.970
This has never happened to me before, but I sat in the office.
我以前从未遇到过这种情况，我坐在办公室里。

339
00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:33.670
And as I was there waiting to meet the showrunner,
就在我等着见剧集主创的时候，

340
00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:36.510
they got the call that the pilot hadn't been picked up to series.
他们接到了电话，说试播集没有被预订成正式剧集。

341
00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.970
So I sat there and then the assistant came out and was like,
所以我坐在那里，然后助理出来说，

342
00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:40.790
you should go home.
你应该回家了。

343
00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:42.090
Like, there's no jobs.
因为已经没有工作机会了。

344
00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.310
And so I just like got up and left.
于是我就起身离开了。

345
00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:48.590
And then the second one was at the office with Greg Daniels.
第二个面试是格雷格·丹尼尔斯负责的《办公室》。

346
00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.230
And so I met with him.
我见了他。

347
00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:53.910
And just so you know, my agent at the time, who I won't mention,
顺便提一下，我当时的经纪人——我就不提名字了——

348
00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:57.710
was really like, yeah, this show doesn't have a lot of heat.
当时真的说，这部剧没什么热度。

349
00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.630
Like, I don't think it's really going to do anything.
我觉得它不会有什么起色。

350
00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.290
Everyone likes the British one better.
大家都觉得英版更好看。

351
00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.530
So it's just like, you know, it's good to meet Greg Daniels.
所以就是，你知道，能见到格雷格·丹尼尔斯真好。

352
00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.770
He's like done a lot of good stuff.
他做过很多优秀的作品。

353
00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:08.690
But like, it's just good.
但就是，感觉很好。

354
00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.070
It's just good to like have a general.
能有个总负责人感觉真好。

355
00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:13.010
So I went in there and there was not a lot of stakes.
所以我去面试的时候，其实没什么压力。

356
00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:19.230
And I had a very, a really fun interview with Greg that lasted two hours.
我和格雷格进行了一次非常、非常有趣的面试，持续了两个小时。

357
00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.270
But you guys know Greg.
但你们都了解格雷格。

358
00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:23.590
So it was actually probably only 15 minutes of talking in two hours.
所以实际上两个小时里可能只有15分钟是在谈正事。

359
00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:29.950
And, and then I, he hired me and, or he didn't, he didn't hire me in the meeting.
然后，他雇用了我，或者说，他当时并没有在面试中直接雇用我。

360
00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:34.110
Like they still had to do upfronts and everything, but we had a great meeting and I heard it went well.
他们还得做预售发布会之类的，但我们谈得很愉快，我听说结果不错。

361
00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:39.430
And then like a month and a half later, I was told I was coming back for six episodes, such a small first season.
大概一个半月后，我被告知要回来写六集剧本，第一季真是太短了。

362
00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:46.990
But I was so new and I think you guys were, you know, new enough too, that it was just like, oh my gosh, any episodes, that's fantastic.
但我当时是个新人，我想你们当时也足够新，所以感觉就是，天哪，能有剧集写真是太棒了。

363
00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:52.810
Not knowing that that was kind of an unusually small number of episodes, but that was, that was how I got on the office.
当时并不知道这集数少得不寻常，但这就是我加入《办公室》的过程。

364
00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:56.730
And how did you end up then playing a role on the show?
那你后来是怎么在剧中扮演角色的呢？

365
00:17:56.730 --> 00:18:08.710
So, you know, he had put, Greg had put into the contract, these acting, these writing contract, these acting clauses for, I think a number of the writers, at least it was in mine.
格雷格在合同里，在编剧合同里，加入了一些表演条款，我想是针对很多编剧的，至少我的合同里有。

366
00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:16.830
And I think Paul Lieberstein's, so I guess in the back of his mind, he was thinking in those terms, but the first season classic episode, Diversity Day,
我想保罗·利伯斯坦的合同里也有，所以我想他当时心里已经有这个打算了，但第一季的经典剧集《多元文化日》，

367
00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.430
written by the great BJ Novak.
是由伟大的BJ·诺瓦克写的。

368
00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:27.190
Um, I remember in the room, he loved this idea, Greg loved this idea of Michael Scott offending all these people, but it's like, it's,
我记得在编剧室里，他很喜欢这个点子，格雷格很喜欢迈克尔·斯科特冒犯所有人的这个点子，但就像是，

369
00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:32.490
it's kind of the funniest version of it when there's like some minority people there too, who can get extra offended.
当现场有一些少数族裔在场，能表现出更强烈的被冒犯感时，这才是最搞笑的版本。

370
00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:37.810
So at that time, I think it just made sense to have another minority person.
所以当时，我觉得再多一个少数族裔角色是很合理的。

371
00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:39.990
And I was like, I'll do it.
我就说，我来演吧。

372
00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:41.130
I actually, I didn't volunteer.
其实，我并没有主动请缨。

373
00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:44.810
He's like, he's, I had two lines in that episode and he said, do you want to be in it?
他当时，我有两句台词，他问我，你想演吗？

374
00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:45.650
And I was like, of course.
我说，当然想。

375
00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:49.270
Um, and so Diversity Day, yeah, thank heavens.
所以《多元文化日》，天哪，谢天谢地。

376
00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.210
That was the second episode.
那是第二集。

377
00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.930
Cause then that guest starred then.
因为从那之后我就开始客串了。

378
00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:56.790
And I think maybe once or twice that first season, I wasn't in it very much.
我想第一季里我大概演了一两次，戏份不多。

379
00:18:56.930 --> 00:19:02.430
And then second season was like, I sort of saw, I got more lines and yeah, that's how it happened.
到了第二季，我发现我的台词变多了，是的，事情就是这样发生的。

380
00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:06.150
What blew me away, Mindy, is when I think back on that.
明迪，让我感到震惊的是，当我回想起那段时光时。

381
00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:12.410
And I was, I was sort of reading back on, you know, Wikipedia about all of us and where we were at in our lives at that time.
我当时在维基百科上读到关于我们所有人的信息，以及我们当时在生活中的处境。

382
00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:17.490
And you were 24 and that blows my mind.
你当时才24岁，这让我感到不可思议。

383
00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:24.750
You're, you had your act together for, to me, for someone at 24, you, you, you were amazing.
你当时就已经很有条理了，对我来说，对于一个24岁的人，你真的很了不起。

384
00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:29.130
Cause at 24, I was, um, I think I was doing takeout at Chin Chin's.
因为我在24岁的时候，我想我还在Chin Chin餐厅做外卖打包工作。

385
00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:30.790
Um, I wasn't a waiter.
我不是服务员。

386
00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:32.870
I was just doing a hostess job.
我只是个带位员。

387
00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:34.230
Do you know, you know what it is?
你知道那是什么工作吗？

388
00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.250
Well, thank you for saying that.
嗯，谢谢你这么说。

389
00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:39.310
I mean, I love to feel like I was a wonder kid, but you know what it is?
我是说，我很想觉得自己是个天才少年，但你知道是怎么回事吗？

390
00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:43.270
Is that it's just the life of a writer, a comedy writer and the life of an actor.
这就是编剧，喜剧编剧和演员的生活。

391
00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:45.690
They're just so, they're so different, right?
它们太不一样了，对吧？

392
00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:51.230
Like it's so, it's very hard to break into comedy writing, but I do think that is easier than breaking into acting.
进入喜剧编剧行业很难，但我认为这比进入演艺圈要容易。

393
00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:58.790
Because if you can write, you can write your own opportunities and write a spec script that, you know, then you can use and send out.
因为如果你会写，你就能创造自己的机会，写一个样片剧本，然后你可以用它去投稿。

394
00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:03.610
Whereas like when you're a young actor, you're like, I just hope someone calls me in to see something.
而当你是一个年轻演员时，你会想，我只希望有人能叫我去试镜。

395
00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:05.130
So thank you for saying that.
所以谢谢你这么说。

396
00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:13.650
But, you know, it also, it felt less special because BJ's there and he was the same age and he'd already written on a show at 24.
但你知道，这也让我觉得没那么特别了，因为BJ也在那里，他和我同岁，而且他在24岁时就已经给一部剧写过剧本了。

397
00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:15.030
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

398
00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:18.190
So it's just when I was like, oh, I guess I'm like young and cool.
所以当我还在想，哦，我大概很年轻很酷吧。

399
00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.110
He was like, oh yeah, I've already worked on,
他却说，哦，是的，我已经参与过，

400
00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:28.690
he was on a Bob Saget sitcom and Mike Schur was like 28 and had already had like an Emmy and been at SNL for nine years or something crazy.
他当时在鲍勃·萨格特的剧组里，而迈克·舒尔当时才28岁，就已经拿过艾美奖，并在《周六夜现场》待了九年，简直疯狂。

401
00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:36.990
So there was no sense of like, you could ever think you were special or like ahead of the curve or anything like that with that group of people.
所以在那群人里，你根本不会觉得自己有什么特别，或者比别人领先什么的。

402
00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.810
Well, I always thought you were special.
嗯，我一直觉得你很特别。

403
00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:39.370
Thank you.
谢谢你。

404
00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:40.270
Thanks, Angela.
谢谢，安吉拉。

405
00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:42.230
All right.
好吧。

406
00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.010
Should we get into this episode, Jenna?
我们要开始聊这一集了吗，珍娜？

407
00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:44.310
Yeah.
好啊。

408
00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:44.870
Yes.
好的。

409
00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.930
Did you get a chance to rewatch it?
你有机会重温这一集了吗？

410
00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:47.670
Yes, I did.
是的，看了。

411
00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:50.470
What was it like for you to rewatch it?
重温这一集对你来说是什么感觉？

412
00:20:51.470 --> 00:21:00.570
I, I have to say, I feel really lucky that Greg wanted to do this episode because it feels like now, you know, we,
我，我不得不说，我觉得自己真的很幸运，格雷格想做这一集，因为感觉现在，你知道，我们，

413
00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:06.550
Angela was on my most recent show and we did an episode about Ganesh Puja and there's so much more, you know,
安吉拉参加了我最近的节目，我们做了一期关于象神节的节目，还有很多，你知道，

414
00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:10.050
there's so many more shows on the air with like diverse casts and everything.
现在电视上有很多演员阵容多元的节目，诸如此类的。

415
00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:15.750
But the fact that on primetime television and I don't know what year did it come out, 2007, maybe?
但事实上，在黄金时段的电视节目中——我不知道是哪一年播出的，2007年吗？

416
00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:18.370
It aired November 2nd, 2006.
它是在2006年11月2日播出的。

417
00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:26.650
It was seen by 8.8 million people and it was the first American television comedy series to depict the Hindu festival of Diwali.
当时有880万人收看，它是第一部描绘印度排灯节的美国电视喜剧系列剧。

418
00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:28.250
It was the very first one.
确实是第一部。

419
00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.250
That's cool.
那太酷了。

420
00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:30.830
That's amazing.
太棒了。

421
00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.730
Go us for doing that.
为我们能做到这一点点赞。

422
00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:36.070
And, you know, the show Mindy's referring to is Never Have I Ever.
而且，你知道，明迪提到的那个节目是《好想做一次》。

423
00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:43.990
However, Mindy, I do want to give it a little plug here because it's so great and, and the cast is great and you're with them from the beginning.
不过，明迪，我确实想在这里给它打个小广告，因为它太棒了，演员阵容也很棒，你从一开始就和他们在一起。

424
00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:47.650
The, the young actors you got, I felt a hundred years old on that set.
那些年轻演员，我在片场觉得自己都一百岁了。

425
00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:48.970
So did I.
我也是。

426
00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.250
So did everyone.
大家都是。

427
00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:52.150
So did everyone who wasn't 17.
所有不是17岁的人都这么觉得。

428
00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:53.270
Oh my God.
天哪。

429
00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:53.590
With you.
跟你一样。

430
00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:56.310
And they were so cute and they love The Office so much.
他们太可爱了，而且他们非常喜欢《办公室》这部剧。

431
00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:56.990
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

432
00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:58.730
They were so starstruck by you, Angela.
他们见到你时都被惊呆了，安吉拉。

433
00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.270
It was so special that you got to be there.
你能去那里真是太特别了。

434
00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:01.070
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

435
00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:03.330
Mindy, what is the name of the lead actress on that show?
明迪，那个节目的女主角叫什么名字？

436
00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:04.870
Maitreyi Ramakrishnan.
麦特里·拉马克里斯南。

437
00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:06.830
I adore her.
我太喜欢她了。

438
00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:07.470
Oh.
哦。

439
00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:12.870
I, cause when you watch the show, you are so immediately in with her journey.
我，因为当你观看这部剧时，你会立刻沉浸在她的旅程中。

440
00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:13.710
Immediately.
立刻。

441
00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:19.710
She is so like effervescent and open and just, wow, what a find.
她真是太活泼、太开朗了，哇，真是个了不起的发现。

442
00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:20.390
What a find.
真是个了不起的发现。

443
00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:20.610
Thank you.
谢谢。

444
00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.110
She's going to flip out.
她一定会乐疯的。

445
00:22:22.330 --> 00:22:25.330
She, Jenna, she's, The Office is her number one favorite show.
她，珍娜，她，《办公室》是她最喜欢的剧。

446
00:22:25.430 --> 00:22:32.630
If you go on her social media for more than two days, there's like an Office meme or there's like, yeah, I bet you've been on her Instagram.
如果你翻翻她的社交媒体，不出两天就能看到《办公室》的梗图，或者，是的，我敢打赌你肯定看过她的Instagram。

447
00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:35.590
Like, please don't throw trash at me.
比如，请别往我身上扔垃圾。

448
00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:38.930
Like, just like some famous Pam line.
就像帕姆的一些经典台词。

449
00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:41.590
Okay, so here we go.
好了，我们开始吧。

450
00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:44.450
So now we have Diwali, the Festival of Lights.
那么现在，我们来聊聊排灯节，也就是光明节。

451
00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:45.850
It's on network TV.
这可是电视网播出的节目。

452
00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:55.990
Mindy, you have been so amazing at just really, I feel like, representing all different sides of culture and on television.
敏迪，你真的太了不起了，我觉得你确实在电视上展现了多元文化的方方面面。

453
00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:59.550
It's just, you should know what it's meant to people.
你真的应该知道这对人们意味着什么。

454
00:22:59.550 --> 00:23:08.190
We had a lot of people write in about having their community seen in this mainstream way what it meant to them.
很多人写信告诉我们，看到他们的社区以这种主流方式被呈现出来，对他们来说意义重大。

455
00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:09.010
It's really moving.
这真的很感人。

456
00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:09.410
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

457
00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:10.510
That's so nice.
太暖心了。

458
00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:17.210
I mean, you know, the one of the harder things about when you write the Diwali episode is like, we couldn't believe that Greg said yes.
我是说，你知道，写排灯节那一集最难的事情之一就是，我们简直不敢相信格雷格竟然答应了。

459
00:23:17.350 --> 00:23:20.730
Cause normally we would do like a Halloween episode at that time of year cause it's the end of October.
因为通常在那个时节，也就是十月底，我们会拍万圣节特辑。

460
00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:26.730
But then I, when he said yes, I had to kind of confront the fact that I'm Indian American.
但当他答应之后，我不得不面对一个事实，那就是我虽然是印度裔美国人，

461
00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:28.990
I don't know very much about the holiday.
但我对这个节日其实了解不多。

462
00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:38.890
And that that experience of being Indian American and talking about how you don't know very much about the holiday kind of became a big part of the episode, which I loved.
而那种作为印度裔美国人却对节日知之甚少的经历，反而成了那一集的重要组成部分，我非常喜欢这一点。

463
00:23:38.990 --> 00:23:41.770
I didn't, I liked that Greg thought that was just as interesting,
我喜欢格雷格认为这一点同样有趣，

464
00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:48.970
if not more interesting than me going and like pretending that like my family and I were these experts at Hindu holidays and everything.
甚至比我假装我和我的家人是印度教节日专家之类的要有趣得多。

465
00:23:48.970 --> 00:23:57.850
So I really liked that Kelly is, is, has this defiant attitude about it, that it's really important while also not knowing anything about it at all.
所以我真的很喜欢凯莉那种反叛的态度，她觉得这很重要，但同时又对它一无所知。

466
00:23:58.270 --> 00:23:58.750
Yes.
没错。

467
00:23:58.890 --> 00:24:02.290
Except that she gets to wear a, like an outfit that has some sparkles on it.
除了她能穿上一套带亮片的衣服之外。

468
00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:02.750
Yes.
是的。

469
00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:03.450
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

470
00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:06.130
And the music part, she's really excited about that.
还有音乐部分，她对此感到非常兴奋。

471
00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:06.770
Yeah.
是啊。

472
00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:13.610
And Michael in the cold open, I mean, Mindy, I love whenever Steve would do an impression of us as our characters.
还有开场戏里的迈克尔，我是说，敏迪，我超爱史蒂夫模仿我们角色的样子。

473
00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:14.310
Yes.
我也是。

474
00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:19.250
And so Michael's like, well, if you ask Kelly, it's like, blah, blah, super fun.
迈克尔当时说，如果你去问凯莉，她会说，巴拉巴拉，超级好玩。

475
00:24:21.590 --> 00:24:25.090
Yes, that, that, I know, and he didn't get to do that that much, right?
没错，我知道，他其实没怎么做过这种模仿，对吧？

476
00:24:25.250 --> 00:24:29.550
Like, I felt like that he didn't do impressions of us too, too much.
我觉得他模仿我们的次数并不多。

477
00:24:29.870 --> 00:24:32.510
I, when he did, I just, it just got me so tickled.
每当他模仿的时候，我都会被逗得不行。

478
00:24:32.750 --> 00:24:34.010
I know, it was so funny.
我知道，真的太搞笑了。

479
00:24:34.230 --> 00:24:38.090
I have a gazillion things I want to say, Jenna, but go, go, you go.
珍娜，我有无数话想说，但你先说，你先说。

480
00:24:38.090 --> 00:24:46.010
Oh, one of my favorite lines in this whole episode is this, how long have you been married to the cheerleader?
噢，这一整集里我最喜欢的台词之一就是这句：你和那个啦啦队长结婚多久了？

481
00:24:47.450 --> 00:24:48.950
And that was your dad.
那是你爸爸演的。

482
00:24:49.350 --> 00:24:50.130
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

483
00:24:50.330 --> 00:24:54.050
To this day, my dad gets checks from, he gets residual checks.
直到今天，我爸爸还能收到《办公室》的重播版税支票。

484
00:24:54.350 --> 00:24:56.490
It's like his, the thing he's the most proud of.
这简直是他最引以为傲的事情了。

485
00:24:56.970 --> 00:24:58.350
Oh, from the office?
噢，是因为《办公室》吗？

486
00:24:58.630 --> 00:24:59.910
Yes, of course, right?
是啊，当然了，对吧？

487
00:25:00.150 --> 00:25:00.470
Yeah.
没错。

488
00:25:00.470 --> 00:25:08.010
And one time he was with my stepmom at Erewhon and they got stopped and someone was like, you were in the office, weren't you?
有一次他和我的继母在Erewhon超市，被人拦住问：你是《办公室》里的那个人吧？

489
00:25:08.190 --> 00:25:10.990
And that was like early when they were dating before they got married.
那还是他们刚开始约会还没结婚的时候。

490
00:25:10.990 --> 00:25:13.650
And my dad was like, felt so cool about it.
我爸爸当时觉得酷毙了。

491
00:25:14.250 --> 00:25:17.670
So, yeah, that was like some good, like street cred right there.
所以，没错，那确实让他很有面子。

492
00:25:17.830 --> 00:25:18.790
I'm being recognized.
我被认出来了。

493
00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:20.130
Yeah, completely.
完全同意。

494
00:25:20.430 --> 00:25:24.250
I just remember that that was like those episodes, you know, at the beginning of the season,
我记得在季初的那些剧集里，

495
00:25:24.250 --> 00:25:30.850
it felt like one thing we did a lot was somehow we pulled out someone from the main cast and there was somebody somewhere else.
我们经常做的一件事就是把某个主要角色从剧组抽离出来，让他们去别的地方。

496
00:25:30.870 --> 00:25:33.010
And that was Stanford for that season.
那一季就是斯坦福大学那条线。

497
00:25:33.630 --> 00:25:33.990
Yes.
没错。

498
00:25:34.110 --> 00:25:36.750
And it was one of those ones where I really liked the Stanford episodes.
我真的很喜欢斯坦福的那几集。

499
00:25:36.910 --> 00:25:39.010
I think sometimes when we did that, it worked really well.
我觉得有时候我们这样做效果非常好。

500
00:25:39.150 --> 00:25:41.270
Sometimes when we pulled them out, we were like, oh, just come back.
但有时候把他们抽离出来，我们又会想，噢，还是让他们回来吧。

501
00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:42.950
We just like want you back in the main caSt.
我们只是想让你回到主要演员阵容中。

502
00:25:43.250 --> 00:25:46.670
But that was a time where I felt like it, it worked pretty well.
但那段时间我觉得，效果还挺不错的。

503
00:25:46.910 --> 00:25:52.510
And I remember thinking, cause I was like, at the beginning, I was like, what were like, what was like Ed and John doing?
我记得当时在想，因为起初我在想，埃德和约翰他们到底在干什么？

504
00:25:52.730 --> 00:25:53.910
And I was like, oh, they weren't there.
然后我意识到，哦，他们当时不在那儿。

505
00:25:54.250 --> 00:25:54.710
Yeah.
是啊。

506
00:25:54.890 --> 00:25:58.750
So it was, it was fun to just, I forgot about that whole thing.
所以那很有趣，我差点把整件事都忘了。

507
00:25:58.870 --> 00:26:04.510
And I remember what I really liked about Stanford was like, that was a really funny group of people there.
我记得我真的很喜欢斯坦福分部，因为那里有一群特别有趣的人。

508
00:26:04.670 --> 00:26:07.690
Even the people that didn't have big parts, like in the Stanford branch.
即使是那些戏份不多的人，在斯坦福分部也是如此。

509
00:26:08.030 --> 00:26:08.450
Yeah.
没错。

510
00:26:08.810 --> 00:26:12.570
Those, I just thought we nailed those prototypes or whatever.
那些，我真觉得我们把那些原型人物刻画得太到位了。

511
00:26:12.730 --> 00:26:14.790
Like I was never bored when I had to go over there.
我每次去那边的时候从来没觉得无聊过。

512
00:26:14.990 --> 00:26:16.570
No, it was so well done.
确实，做得太棒了。

513
00:26:16.790 --> 00:26:23.770
We talked a little bit about having over on the Scranton set, like Angela and I having a little bit of like FOMO
我们之前聊过，在斯克兰顿片场时，安吉拉和我有点那种错失恐惧症（FOMO），

514
00:26:23.770 --> 00:26:28.070
and jealousy of how much fun they were having over on Stanford because everybody was so funny.
嫉妒他们在斯坦福那边玩得那么开心，因为每个人都太搞笑了。

515
00:26:28.070 --> 00:26:31.450
And also they would only have to work like one and a half days a week.
而且他们每周只需要工作一天半左右。

516
00:26:31.670 --> 00:26:31.950
That's right.
没错。

517
00:26:32.250 --> 00:26:34.830
Super relaxed and just like having the best time.
超级轻松，简直玩得太开心了。

518
00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:36.210
And then they got four days off.
然后他们还能休四天假。

519
00:26:36.330 --> 00:26:40.650
And we were, we were just like, hey, I forgot about that.
我们当时就觉得，嘿，我都忘了这茬了。

520
00:26:40.650 --> 00:26:45.930
Well, Jenna, the best example of that was the Michael Scott Paper Company, which was like,
珍娜，最好的例子就是“迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司”那段剧情，就像是，

521
00:26:45.930 --> 00:26:46.130
Oh yeah.
哦，对。

522
00:26:46.390 --> 00:26:50.330
Which was like, to me, the, one of my favorite arcs we've ever done.
对我来说，那是我最喜欢的剧情线之一。

523
00:26:50.450 --> 00:26:54.670
And I don't think I wrote any of the episodes for you guys there, but like it has, I think,
虽然我觉得我没给你们写过那部分的剧集，但我觉得，

524
00:26:54.870 --> 00:27:00.650
that pairing of people, that group of people on their mission was like one of the times where I was like,
那群人组合在一起执行任务的时候，是我觉得，

525
00:27:00.750 --> 00:27:04.670
wow, this is just like equally, if not more funny than like anything that's going,
哇，这简直和任何其他剧情一样，甚至比其他剧情更有趣，

526
00:27:04.830 --> 00:27:07.230
wait, and that's when Idris Elba was, was that?
等等，那是伊德里斯·艾尔巴在的时候吗？

527
00:27:07.230 --> 00:27:07.590
Yeah.
是啊。

528
00:27:07.910 --> 00:27:08.210
Yeah.
没错。

529
00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:11.550
Well, I mean, I guess if, if you cut back to Idris Elba, you're doing fine.
我是说，我觉得只要有伊德里斯·艾尔巴在，你们的表现就不会差。

530
00:27:11.750 --> 00:27:11.910
Yeah.
没错。

531
00:27:12.490 --> 00:27:14.630
I loved being in Michael Scott Paper Company.
我超爱“迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司”那段经历。

532
00:27:14.850 --> 00:27:15.390
Oh my God.
天哪。

533
00:27:15.550 --> 00:27:17.230
I kind of didn't want that arc to end.
我甚至有点不想让那段剧情结束。

534
00:27:17.430 --> 00:27:19.270
And Vikram, the four of you together.
还有维克拉姆，你们四个人在一起的时候。

535
00:27:19.470 --> 00:27:20.130
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

536
00:27:20.210 --> 00:27:20.370
Yeah.
是啊。

537
00:27:20.870 --> 00:27:21.230
Amazing.
太棒了。

538
00:27:21.450 --> 00:27:23.790
It was so, it was like, it could have been its own movie.
真的，那简直可以拍成一部独立的电影。

539
00:27:23.930 --> 00:27:26.090
Like I know we're not talking about the Michael Scott Paper Company right now.
我知道我们现在讨论的不是“迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司”。

540
00:27:26.170 --> 00:27:29.790
We're talking about Diwali, but it felt like it was his own Bad News Bears type movie.
我们在聊“排灯节”，但那感觉就像是一部属于他们自己的《少棒闯天下》式的电影。

541
00:27:30.590 --> 00:27:32.010
But you're, you're right, Mindy.
但你是对的，敏迪。

542
00:27:32.110 --> 00:27:37.090
There were these pairings that would happen that were just as pure and beautiful as what was happening in Scranton.
确实会出现一些组合，它们和斯克兰顿发生的故事一样纯粹而美好。

543
00:27:37.090 --> 00:27:40.810
And, you know, I got the DVD box set and I watched the deleted scenes.
而且，你知道，我买了DVD套装，看了里面的删减片段。

544
00:27:40.810 --> 00:27:44.690
And there's so many scenes at Stanford that never made it in.
斯坦福分部有很多没能放进正片的场景。

545
00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:49.570
And like, there's the, the character that's like always, like was always breastfeeding.
比如那个总是，总是处于哺乳期的角色。

546
00:27:50.130 --> 00:27:50.670
Oh yeah.
哦，对。

547
00:27:51.030 --> 00:27:51.550
Hannah.
汉娜。

548
00:27:52.030 --> 00:27:52.550
Yes.
没错。

549
00:27:52.770 --> 00:27:54.550
Hannah would make Jim really uncomfortable.
汉娜总是让吉姆感到非常尴尬。

550
00:27:54.550 --> 00:28:02.230
And then as far as this episode, I do have a question for you because I was texting with Rashida and she was like, this is the episode.
至于这一集，我有个问题想问你，因为我刚才在和拉什达发短信，她说，就是这一集。

551
00:28:02.390 --> 00:28:09.010
I was so worried everyone was going to hate me because Jim and Karen have this sloppy makeout out in the parking lot.
我当时特别担心大家会讨厌我，因为吉姆和凯伦在停车场有一场那种邋遢的亲热戏。

552
00:28:09.110 --> 00:28:09.510
Yeah.
是啊。

553
00:28:09.910 --> 00:28:10.550
Like a tipsy makeout.
就像那种喝醉了之后的亲热。

554
00:28:10.550 --> 00:28:12.110
It's not in the deleted scenes.
删减片段里也没有。

555
00:28:12.490 --> 00:28:14.290
It didn't even make that cut.
甚至都没进那个剪辑版本。

556
00:28:14.470 --> 00:28:16.210
It was in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里是有这一段的。

557
00:28:16.490 --> 00:28:17.070
Oh yeah.
哦，没错。

558
00:28:17.550 --> 00:28:19.870
Did Rashida, did you guys end up shooting that?
拉什达，你们最后拍那场戏了吗？

559
00:28:19.970 --> 00:28:21.610
Because I was going to ask about that too.
因为我也正想问这个呢。

560
00:28:22.110 --> 00:28:30.370
When I was going, I have the shooting draft from this episode and I went back and I read it and I was like, wait, wait, Jim and Karen kiss?
我当时在看这一集的拍摄剧本，读到那儿的时候我就想，等等，吉姆和凯伦接吻了？

561
00:28:30.770 --> 00:28:30.950
Yeah.
是啊。

562
00:28:31.130 --> 00:28:31.590
They're kissing?
他们在接吻？

563
00:28:31.650 --> 00:28:32.810
Why are they making out?
他们为什么要亲热？

564
00:28:33.030 --> 00:28:36.030
But then it's nowhere in the episode and it's not in the deleted scenes.
但后来这一集里完全没出现，删减片段里也没有。

565
00:28:36.030 --> 00:28:43.630
Well, I have a, my memory, even though I was the writer on set, obviously for the episode, I have like zero memory of that.
嗯，我的记忆是，尽管我当时是那一集的现场编剧，但我对那场戏完全没印象。

566
00:28:44.170 --> 00:28:51.570
But I will say that one thing that we used to do, I felt a lot was to write scripts that advance story.
但我得说，我们以前常做的一件事，我觉得挺多的，就是写那些推动剧情发展的剧本。

567
00:28:51.830 --> 00:28:58.690
And then what we'd noticed when we only had 21 and a half minutes to air an episode that such like a little went such a long way.
后来我们发现，当一集节目只有21分半的播出时间时，一点点铺垫就能起到很大的作用。

568
00:28:58.690 --> 00:29:07.370
Like if there is an attractive woman who is working in the new environment and she seems to have some kind of rapport with Jim or together they're making fun of Andy, you're like,
比如如果有一个有吸引力的女性在新的环境里工作，她似乎和吉姆很投缘，或者他们一起取笑安迪，你就会觉得，

569
00:29:07.550 --> 00:29:09.570
oh, that's interesting.
哦，这很有意思。

570
00:29:09.850 --> 00:29:10.870
Like that might be something.
感觉这可能会发展出点什么。

571
00:29:11.170 --> 00:29:15.950
And so it felt like we were always like pulling back that stuff.
所以感觉我们总是会把那些东西往回撤一点。

572
00:29:15.950 --> 00:29:25.250
Like Jenna, don't you feel like you shot a lot of stuff with, with John that was like, not like, cause you guys weren't like super flirty in those early seasons,
珍娜，你不觉得你和约翰拍了很多戏，不是那种，因为你们在早期几季里并不是特别调情，

573
00:29:25.390 --> 00:29:28.590
like overtly flirty, but like that you'd watch it and you're like, oh, this was like, they,
不是那种明目张胆的调情，但你看的时候会觉得，哦，这就像是，他们，

574
00:29:28.590 --> 00:29:34.730
they used like less than I thought they would in terms of like showing your guys' like budding romance.
他们用的比我想象的要少，在展现你们那种萌芽中的恋情方面。

575
00:29:35.270 --> 00:29:35.750
Yes.
是的。

576
00:29:35.750 --> 00:29:42.770
And I would also add that there were some scenes where we would get in, I don't know if I would call it fights,
我还要补充一点，有些场景我们确实会产生，我不知道该不该叫争执，

577
00:29:42.770 --> 00:29:51.570
but there were some like disagreements in certain episodes and they would pull back on those two and they, they would make them smaller.
但有些剧集里确实会有一些分歧，他们也会把那些戏份往回撤，把它们处理得更含蓄。

578
00:29:52.130 --> 00:29:54.190
I wonder if it's, it's, it's interesting.
我在想这是否，这挺有意思的。

579
00:29:54.390 --> 00:30:00.190
It's just like for so much of the show in terms of romance, it was always like less is more.
就像这部剧里关于浪漫的部分，总是讲究少即是多。

580
00:30:00.330 --> 00:30:04.110
Whereas for comedy, it was like, let's hoist up Tony Gardner onto the table.
而对于喜剧部分，就像是，让我们把托尼·加德纳抬到桌子上吧。

581
00:30:07.990 --> 00:30:12.690
But for all that stuff, it was, yeah, just a little goes a long way.
但对于所有那些情感戏，确实是，一点点铺垫就足够了。

582
00:30:13.050 --> 00:30:15.890
But the relationships were so finessed.
但那些人际关系处理得非常巧妙。

583
00:30:15.970 --> 00:30:17.550
I thought they were so smartly done.
我觉得它们做得非常聪明。

584
00:30:17.550 --> 00:30:26.610
One of the things I remember really well about this episode was again, like it's such a time capsule of like 2006 or whatever, because the love interest,
关于这一集我记得很清楚的一件事是，它就像是2006年左右的时间胶囊，因为那个追求者，

585
00:30:27.010 --> 00:30:32.090
he wasn't really a love interest, but there was an Indian character who my parents preferred to Ryan.
他其实算不上追求者，但有一个印度裔角色，我父母比瑞安更喜欢他。

586
00:30:32.350 --> 00:30:33.750
That was like a very small part of it.
那只是其中很小的一部分。

587
00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:42.350
And it was played by this writer, Vali Chandrasekharan, who was kind of a friend of the writers on the show, but not an actor, just a guy, like a guy we knew.
扮演他的是编剧瓦利·钱德拉塞卡兰，他算是剧组编剧们的朋友，不是演员，只是个普通人，我们认识的一个人。

588
00:30:42.470 --> 00:30:46.990
There was a real sort of casualness to our show of like, we're just kind of putting it together.
我们的剧有一种真正的随意感，就像是，我们只是凑合着把它做出来。

589
00:30:46.990 --> 00:30:47.450
Yeah.
是啊。

590
00:30:47.730 --> 00:30:48.830
We probably shot this.
我们大概拍了这个。

591
00:30:48.970 --> 00:30:50.490
This is season three, right?
这是第三季，对吧？

592
00:30:51.170 --> 00:30:54.510
For Diwali, it was, we knew that season two had done well.
对于排灯节那一集，我们知道第二季表现不错。

593
00:30:54.670 --> 00:30:57.630
I don't, we'd been nominated probably at this point when we were shooting.
我不知道，我们拍摄的时候可能已经获得提名了。

594
00:30:57.870 --> 00:30:59.490
We'd been nominated, but we didn't know.
我们被提名了，但我们当时不知道。

595
00:30:59.630 --> 00:31:07.830
So I felt like now, I felt like at the beginning of season three, when we started shooting, we started feeling like a little bit more like, okay,
所以我感觉现在，我觉得在第三季刚开始拍摄的时候，我们开始感觉好一点了，觉得，好吧，

596
00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:10.370
we're not going to just get canceled or something.
我们不会轻易被砍掉什么的。

597
00:31:10.370 --> 00:31:20.590
Um, because I remember so much stress earlier on thinking like, it's hard to enjoy a show as much when you're like, is this even going to last?
嗯，因为我记得早期有很多压力，觉得当你担心这剧能不能撑下去时，很难真正享受拍摄过程。

598
00:31:21.010 --> 00:31:26.770
And I do remember being able to enjoy things a little bit more starting like at the beginning of season three.
我确实记得从第三季开始，我能更多地享受拍摄过程了。

599
00:31:27.210 --> 00:31:30.470
Sorry, I just keep going off of, cause I'm, I don't get to talk about the office that much.
抱歉，我一直在跑题，因为我平时没机会聊《办公室》。

600
00:31:30.510 --> 00:31:35.730
I just, I'm talking really like, like holistically about the show instead of just about this episode.
我只是，我是在从整体上谈论这部剧，而不是只谈这一集。

601
00:31:35.730 --> 00:31:40.490
But don't worry, we're going to break down this whole episode and like, get into the nitty gritty of it.
不过别担心，我们会详细拆解这一整集，深入探讨其中的细节。

602
00:31:40.490 --> 00:31:42.830
So this can be your office memories.
所以这可以成为你们关于《办公室》的回忆。

603
00:31:42.990 --> 00:31:45.170
There's no prescription for what we talk about.
我们聊的内容没有固定的章法。

604
00:31:45.350 --> 00:31:45.610
Yeah.
没错。

605
00:31:45.870 --> 00:31:46.290
Okay, cool.
好的，太棒了。

606
00:31:46.450 --> 00:31:53.690
Greg was on to talk about booze cruise and we just, we went everywhere, you know, but that's, it's such a special chapter in all of our lives.
格雷格之前来聊过“游轮派对”那一集，我们聊得天南地北，但那一集确实是我们所有人生命中非常特别的一个篇章。

607
00:31:53.690 --> 00:31:56.550
I think it's hard to compartmentalize it to one episode.
我觉得很难把它仅仅局限在某一集里。

608
00:31:56.550 --> 00:31:57.990
It's such a big part of us.
它在我们心中占据了很大一部分。

609
00:31:57.990 --> 00:32:08.870
You know, one of the things I remember a lot about doing the office was we didn't realize as writers, how rare it was for Greg to just say, okay, well,
你知道，关于拍摄《办公室》，我印象很深的一点是，作为编剧，我们当时没意识到格雷格的做法有多罕见，他会直接说，好吧，

610
00:32:09.010 --> 00:32:12.270
I'm just going to give one person from the writer's world on set.
我就派编剧团队里的一个人去片场。

611
00:32:12.410 --> 00:32:14.130
And that's just going to be the writer of the episode.
那个人就是这一集的编剧。

612
00:32:14.330 --> 00:32:17.130
Some people do that now, but it's usually like an upper level writer.
现在有些人也会这样做，但通常都是资深编剧。

613
00:32:17.430 --> 00:32:23.010
So it's your job to make sure that the intention of the lines is being corrected.
所以你的工作就是确保台词的意图得到准确传达。

614
00:32:23.010 --> 00:32:25.330
Give alts, answer questions from the actors.
提供备选台词，回答演员的问题。

615
00:32:25.730 --> 00:32:27.470
And I was a story editor.
我当时是故事编辑。

616
00:32:27.470 --> 00:32:28.710
When I did this.
我做这一集的时候。

617
00:32:29.190 --> 00:32:31.930
And I remember like, that was pretty stressful.
我记得当时压力挺大的。

618
00:32:32.050 --> 00:32:38.610
I think like, I remember being on the set because Miguel Arteta was not one of our directors that we had all the time.
我记得当时在片场，因为米格尔·阿尔特塔不是我们常驻的导演之一。

619
00:32:38.810 --> 00:32:45.450
And so I remember feeling like, is this like, am I being too like on set?
所以我记得当时心里在想，我是不是太爱在片场晃悠了？

620
00:32:45.550 --> 00:32:47.110
Because we're on location a lot for this episode.
因为这一集我们有很多外景拍摄。

621
00:32:47.110 --> 00:32:49.170
I was like, am I too much in his hair?
我在想，我是不是太碍事了？

622
00:32:49.350 --> 00:32:50.230
Is he going to yell at me?
他会不会冲我发火？

623
00:32:50.530 --> 00:32:54.370
Because I think season one, I was never alone for hot girl.
因为我觉得第一季拍“辣妹”那一集时，我从来没独自去过。

624
00:32:54.370 --> 00:32:57.830
I think Howard and Greg were there for almost all the shooting.
我觉得霍华德和格雷格几乎参与了所有的拍摄。

625
00:32:57.970 --> 00:33:00.230
Because it was, I think, one of the last ones we shot.
因为那好像是我们拍的最后几集之一。

626
00:33:00.490 --> 00:33:07.890
But for this one, it was just like, go, manage set, answer all Indian questions and make sure it's hilarious and do all alts.
但这一集，就像是直接让我去，管理片场，回答所有问题，确保效果爆笑，还要提供所有备选台词。

627
00:33:08.010 --> 00:33:15.710
It's so funny you say that, Mindy, because my impression of you as the writer on set was just always that you were one of my favorites.
明迪，你这么说太有意思了，因为你在片场做编剧时，我一直觉得你是最让我喜欢的编剧之一。

628
00:33:16.050 --> 00:33:16.390
Really?
真的吗？

629
00:33:16.630 --> 00:33:17.390
That's so nice.
太暖心了。

630
00:33:17.390 --> 00:33:17.690
Yes.
是的。

631
00:33:18.210 --> 00:33:21.910
Mostly because you were so up to laugh.
主要是因为你特别爱笑。

632
00:33:22.110 --> 00:33:27.150
Like you found, I always felt like you found everyone hilarious.
我总觉得你觉得每个人都特别搞笑。

633
00:33:27.530 --> 00:33:27.950
Oh my God.
天哪。

634
00:33:28.290 --> 00:33:29.470
You seemed to like everything.
你好像什么都喜欢。

635
00:33:29.650 --> 00:33:31.290
You had the best alts.
你给出的备选台词总是最好的。

636
00:33:31.290 --> 00:33:36.810
So you would sort of throw out ideas, maybe based on something you watched us do.
你会根据我们的表演抛出一些点子。

637
00:33:36.970 --> 00:33:37.690
You'd be like, oh my gosh.
你会说，天哪。

638
00:33:37.810 --> 00:33:38.190
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

639
00:33:38.250 --> 00:33:39.350
Okay, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等，等等，等等，等等。

640
00:33:39.430 --> 00:33:40.270
You have to do that again.
你必须再演一遍那个。

641
00:33:40.430 --> 00:33:41.050
Do that again.
再演一遍。

642
00:33:41.210 --> 00:33:43.030
And then what do you think about saying this?
然后你觉得说这句台词怎么样？

643
00:33:43.030 --> 00:33:43.110
Yes.
对。

644
00:33:43.150 --> 00:33:44.630
And it was like, oh my gosh.
当时的感觉就是，天哪。

645
00:33:44.750 --> 00:33:47.170
It was just like this uplifting, exciting.
那种氛围真的非常振奋人心，令人兴奋。

646
00:33:47.450 --> 00:33:47.890
That's so nice.
太暖心了。

647
00:33:48.190 --> 00:33:49.230
Oh, I loved it.
噢，我太喜欢了。

648
00:33:49.310 --> 00:33:49.770
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

649
00:33:49.870 --> 00:33:51.310
We've talked a lot about that.
我们聊过很多次这个了。

650
00:33:51.490 --> 00:33:53.870
And Jen Salotta was very similar as well.
简·萨洛塔当时也差不多是这样。

651
00:33:54.030 --> 00:33:58.450
Like, well, Jen, you couldn't get, she just would laugh the whole time.
怎么说呢，珍，你根本没法拍，她全程都在笑。

652
00:33:58.590 --> 00:34:00.870
Like, we'd actually have to throw her off because.
我们甚至不得不把她赶走，因为……

653
00:34:01.110 --> 00:34:01.910
She was laughing too much.
她笑得太厉害了。

654
00:34:01.910 --> 00:34:03.610
She would ruin takes, but yeah.
她总是毁掉拍摄，但确实是这样。

655
00:34:03.910 --> 00:34:04.150
Yeah.
没错。

656
00:34:04.330 --> 00:34:13.330
I, I thought we, you know, there's this, this thing that we would do on the show where when a cut would come out, the director's cut, and I've never seen it on any other show,
我……我觉得我们，你知道，剧组有个惯例，每当导演剪辑版出来的时候——我在其他剧组从没见过这种情况——

657
00:34:13.330 --> 00:34:16.210
we would all gather and watch it together in the writer's room.
我们大家都会聚在编剧室一起看。

658
00:34:16.470 --> 00:34:20.870
And director's cuts famously in other shows like make you want to kill yourself.
众所周知，其他剧组的导演剪辑版通常让人想自杀。

659
00:34:21.050 --> 00:34:25.590
They're usually so bad, but the quality was so good because the cast was so good.
它们通常很烂，但我们的质量很高，因为演员阵容太棒了。

660
00:34:25.690 --> 00:34:28.630
And so I remember it was like my favorite time.
所以我记得那是我最喜欢的时光。

661
00:34:28.630 --> 00:34:33.650
We could interrupt all of our work and just go into the little living room area of our writer's room and watch.
我们可以放下手头的工作，直接走进编剧室的小客厅区域观看。

662
00:34:33.730 --> 00:34:34.990
I mean, I was such a fan of the show.
我是说，我真是这部剧的忠实粉丝。

663
00:34:35.090 --> 00:34:40.210
I, I watched almost every cut of every episode and then I would watch it live too.
我几乎看了每一集的每一个剪辑版本，然后播出时我还会再看一遍。

664
00:34:40.390 --> 00:34:45.190
Like I, and I didn't realize how unusual that is for somebody who works on a show.
我是说，我当时没意识到这对剧组工作人员来说有多不寻常。

665
00:34:45.370 --> 00:34:46.650
Most people do it.
大多数人都会看。

666
00:34:46.770 --> 00:34:49.390
And then they, a lot of actors don't even watch it when it airs.
而且，很多演员甚至在剧集播出时都不看。

667
00:34:49.810 --> 00:34:55.850
Um, but I, I really was such a huge fan of the show.
嗯，但我确实是这部剧的超级粉丝。

668
00:34:55.930 --> 00:35:01.250
And a lot of times in those conference room scenes, like I'd have like no lines or one line or something in these four page scenes.
很多时候在那些会议室场景里，我在长达四页的剧本里可能一句台词都没有，或者只有一句。

669
00:35:01.510 --> 00:35:08.290
And to me, it was like going to second city and just watching everyone just be so funny and it just be for free.
对我来说，这就像去了第二城市剧团，免费看着大家表演，而且每个人都那么搞笑。

670
00:35:08.410 --> 00:35:11.930
And you'd be in this like freezing cold room and there'd be snacks every two hours.
你待在那个冷得要命的房间里，每隔两小时还有零食吃。

671
00:35:12.050 --> 00:35:13.730
And I was like, what, how could this be better?
我当时心想，还有比这更好的事吗？

672
00:35:14.730 --> 00:35:17.250
It felt like such an abundance of riches.
这感觉就像拥有了无穷无尽的财富。

673
00:35:17.490 --> 00:35:21.130
I just loved sitting and watching everyone in character, just reacting.
我就是喜欢坐在那儿，看着大家进入角色，看着他们的反应。

674
00:35:21.510 --> 00:35:21.670
Yeah.
没错。

675
00:35:22.090 --> 00:35:24.870
Mindy, I remember one time you were on stage, um,
敏迪，我记得有一次你在舞台上，嗯，

676
00:35:25.050 --> 00:35:35.750
and BJ and you guys were at reception by Jenna and you guys were talking and I walked up and you were having a conversation about some type of like economics.
你和BJ在珍娜的前台那边，你们在聊天，我走过去时，你们正在讨论某种经济学问题。

677
00:35:35.790 --> 00:35:39.590
It was like some kind of like you'd, you'd expanded economics.
就像是某种……你们把经济学给拓展了。

678
00:35:39.590 --> 00:35:43.110
And I walked up and I was like, I'm going to go over here.
我走过去，心想：我还是去别处吧。

679
00:35:43.110 --> 00:35:47.350
I was just like, they are two of the smartest people I've ever met.
我当时觉得，他们是我见过最聪明的两个人。

680
00:35:47.490 --> 00:35:51.010
And I'm going to hard pivot and back away.
我还是赶紧掉头走开吧。

681
00:35:51.410 --> 00:35:53.370
Wait, BJ and I were talking about economics.
等等，BJ和我当时在聊经济学？

682
00:35:53.370 --> 00:35:54.130
We weren't fighting.
我们没在吵架吧？

683
00:35:54.370 --> 00:35:55.370
I'm so surprised.
我太惊讶了。

684
00:35:55.790 --> 00:35:57.910
Oh no, you were, it was a heated discussion.
哦不，你们确实在吵，那是一场激烈的讨论。

685
00:35:58.070 --> 00:35:59.650
You were on opposite sides.
你们各执一词。

686
00:35:59.990 --> 00:36:01.050
That is so funny.
那太搞笑了。

687
00:36:02.070 --> 00:36:10.970
Well, I just, I remember you and Paul and BJ as a little trio, probably because you were the writers who were with the actors.
嗯，我只是记得你、保罗和BJ像个小三人组，可能是因为你们是那些同时担任演员的编剧。

688
00:36:10.970 --> 00:36:17.750
So between takes, you guys would always kind of huddle up and talk like story ideas and like what's happening in the writer's room.
所以在拍摄间隙，你们总是会聚在一起讨论故事构思，或者编剧室里发生的事情。

689
