00:50:09.410 --> 00:50:15.390
So now at four minutes, 23 seconds, Sam, will you play Mustang?
那么现在在4分23秒，山姆，你能播放“野马”那段吗？

971
00:50:16.070 --> 00:50:17.070
Flirty Karen.
调情的凯伦。

972
00:50:17.270 --> 00:50:18.310
Flirty Karen.
调情的凯伦。

973
00:50:18.310 --> 00:50:20.190
That's my mom, Birdie Kinsey.
那是我妈妈，伯迪·金西。

974
00:50:20.390 --> 00:50:21.290
Flirty Karen.
调情的凯伦。

975
00:50:21.890 --> 00:50:24.550
Karen says, hey, nice basket.
凯伦说，嘿，篮子不错。

976
00:50:24.830 --> 00:50:27.430
Ever since the whole chips incident, she's smitten.
自从薯片事件以来，她就迷上他了。

977
00:50:28.150 --> 00:50:28.410
Yep.
没错。

978
00:50:28.850 --> 00:50:35.010
So then Josh comes over and gives Karen the company credit card because they have to work
然后乔什走过来，把公司信用卡给了凯伦，因为他们得加班，

979
00:50:35.010 --> 00:50:37.510
late and they're allowed to buy dinner.
而且他们被允许买晚餐。

980
00:50:37.790 --> 00:50:41.850
But he says, you know, no more than $20 a person this time.
但他说了，你知道，这次每人不超过20美元。

981
00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:44.410
This time, $20 a person.
这次，每人20美元。

982
00:50:44.630 --> 00:50:46.390
We shot this in 2006.
我们是在2006年拍摄的。

983
00:50:48.130 --> 00:50:52.370
Is there a meal out there that you order that's more than $20 a person?
有什么外卖是你点的时候会超过每人20美元的吗？

984
00:50:52.610 --> 00:50:55.130
Hey, maybe there's a reason Stanford doesn't make it.
嘿，也许斯坦福没能成功是有原因的。

985
00:50:56.230 --> 00:50:57.610
I mean, my gosh.
我的天哪。

986
00:50:58.790 --> 00:50:59.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

987
00:51:00.870 --> 00:51:04.370
Maybe I just don't eat at very fancy places for my takeout.
也许我点的外卖都不是什么高档餐厅。

988
00:51:04.530 --> 00:51:11.750
But I feel like I would be challenged to order a meal for more than $20 a person in 2006.
但我觉得在2006年，要点一份超过每人20美元的外卖还挺难的。

989
00:51:12.070 --> 00:51:12.390
Yeah.
是啊。

990
00:51:12.770 --> 00:51:15.390
Especially like late at night in Scranton.
特别是在斯克兰顿的深夜。

991
00:51:15.530 --> 00:51:16.110
What are they getting?
他们能点什么呢？

992
00:51:16.470 --> 00:51:17.870
You know, like Thai food.
你知道，比如泰国菜之类的。

993
00:51:18.030 --> 00:51:18.550
I know.
我知道。

994
00:51:18.990 --> 00:51:19.550
Exactly.
没错。

995
00:51:19.770 --> 00:51:20.630
This is not difficult.
这又不难。

996
00:51:21.510 --> 00:51:24.230
Andy, though, busts out some Jaegermeister.
不过，安迪拿出了野格利口酒。

997
00:51:24.230 --> 00:51:25.830
But he's got other plans.
但他有别的打算。

998
00:51:26.030 --> 00:51:26.870
He's ready to party.
他准备好要狂欢了。

999
00:51:27.070 --> 00:51:33.270
Ed Helms' face when he holds up that Jaegermeister bottle and the shot glasses is hilarious.
艾德·赫尔姆斯举起那瓶野格利口酒和酒杯时的表情太搞笑了。

1000
00:51:34.230 --> 00:51:37.890
You get a window into who Andy was in college and you're like, oh, buddy.
你从中窥见了安迪大学时期的样子，你会想，哦，伙计。

1001
00:51:38.330 --> 00:51:43.410
Well, back in Scranton, things are getting exciting because everyone is showing up to Diwali.
在斯克兰顿，事情变得很有意思，因为大家都来参加排灯节了。

1002
00:51:43.930 --> 00:51:44.810
They're arriving.
他们到了。

1003
00:51:45.030 --> 00:51:45.810
They're walking in.
他们正走进来。

1004
00:51:45.950 --> 00:51:48.110
It's really, really like bright and colorful.
现场真的非常明亮、色彩斑斓。

1005
00:51:48.110 --> 00:51:49.410
And there's music playing.
还有音乐在播放。

1006
00:51:49.650 --> 00:51:52.750
And Phyllis is like, isn't it fun to take our shoes off?
菲利斯说，脱掉鞋子不是很开心吗？

1007
00:51:52.750 --> 00:51:56.710
And Angela's like, I wish not everyone took their shoes off.
安吉拉则说，我真希望不是每个人都脱鞋。

1008
00:51:56.830 --> 00:51:58.050
And Kevin's like, stop it.
凯文说，别说了。

1009
00:51:58.150 --> 00:51:59.630
I told you it was a condition.
我告诉过你这是规定。

1010
00:51:59.990 --> 00:52:08.890
So you guys remember in grief counseling, we talked about a deleted scene that would have been in the episode where Angela and Kevin go off again about his sweaty feet.
大家还记得在哀伤辅导那一集里，我们提到过一个被删减的片段，讲的是安吉拉和凯文又因为他那双汗脚吵起来了。

1011
00:52:09.090 --> 00:52:09.410
Yes.
是的。

1012
00:52:09.410 --> 00:52:11.890
This is a callback to a deleted scene.
这是对那个删减片段的呼应。

1013
00:52:12.210 --> 00:52:16.150
So it's going to go unappreciated by most viewers.
所以大多数观众可能看不出其中的梗。

1014
00:52:16.330 --> 00:52:20.010
But those diehard viewers who watch those deleted scenes will know what this means.
但那些看过删减片段的铁杆粉丝会明白这是什么意思。

1015
00:52:20.050 --> 00:52:26.210
I feel like someone in the writer's room was really determined to make sure we had scenes about Kevin's feet.
我觉得编剧室里肯定有人特别执着于要写关于凯文脚的戏份。

1016
00:52:26.310 --> 00:52:30.710
I feel like it was a note card on the wall that said Kevin's sweaty feet.
我觉得墙上的记事卡上肯定写着“凯文的汗脚”。

1017
00:52:30.710 --> 00:52:34.690
And someone loved it and kept wanting to get it in the episodes.
有人特别喜欢这个点，一直想把它塞进剧集里。

1018
00:52:35.850 --> 00:52:37.830
Well, this is Angela's worst nightmare.
这简直是安吉拉的噩梦。

1019
00:52:38.090 --> 00:52:41.970
People taking off all their shoes, even minus Kevin's sweaty feet.
大家都在脱鞋，就算没有凯文的汗脚也是一样。

1020
00:52:42.030 --> 00:52:45.470
I mean, this is just not how she wants to be at a party.
我是说，这根本不是她想要的派对状态。

1021
00:52:46.030 --> 00:52:47.230
No, no.
没错，没错。

1022
00:52:47.590 --> 00:52:50.610
So, Angela, we got a fan question about these Diwali scenes.
安吉拉，我们收到一个关于排灯节场景的粉丝提问。

1023
00:52:50.750 --> 00:52:52.110
It comes from Sarah Beth Miller.
来自莎拉·贝丝·米勒。

1024
00:52:52.110 --> 00:52:57.350
She asked, was this a real Diwali celebration happening in the filming of this episode?
她问，拍摄这一集时，现场是真的在举行排灯节庆祝活动吗？

1025
00:52:57.690 --> 00:53:01.010
How did you get all of those people in those beautiful costumes?
你们是怎么找来那么多穿着漂亮服装的人的？

1026
00:53:02.150 --> 00:53:03.750
Great question, Sarah Beth.
好问题，莎拉·贝丝。

1027
00:53:04.070 --> 00:53:07.190
I mean, there are so many people in this scene.
这一幕里的人确实非常多。

1028
00:53:07.370 --> 00:53:08.530
So here's the thing.
是这样的。

1029
00:53:08.690 --> 00:53:10.610
It was not a real Diwali festival.
那并不是真正的排灯节。

1030
00:53:11.130 --> 00:53:16.190
That was all put together by our amazing crew, just specifically for this episode.
那全是我们出色的剧组人员专门为这一集搭建出来的。

1031
00:53:16.190 --> 00:53:22.090
Yes, our set designer, Michael Gallenberg, and his team, they decorated that whole gym.
没错，我们的布景设计师迈克尔·加伦伯格和他的团队装饰了整个体育馆。

1032
00:53:22.790 --> 00:53:29.150
Michael had to do a lot of research in order to transform the gymnasium to feel like a real Diwali festival.
迈克尔做了大量的研究，才把体育馆改造成了真正的排灯节现场。

1033
00:53:29.150 --> 00:53:33.010
So I think he would be very proud to know that you wondered if this was real.
我想如果他知道你怀疑这是不是真的，他会感到非常自豪的。

1034
00:53:33.230 --> 00:53:36.410
Like, maybe we just stepped into an existing festival.
就好像我们只是走进了一个现成的节日现场一样。

1035
00:53:36.650 --> 00:53:39.150
No, they made the whole thing.
不，那是他们一手打造的。

1036
00:53:39.290 --> 00:53:40.470
They did a fantastic job.
他们做得太棒了。

1037
00:53:40.670 --> 00:53:44.590
As far as costumes go, my character did not get to dress up, Jenna.
说到服装，我的角色没能打扮，珍娜。

1038
00:53:44.730 --> 00:53:45.610
I was so bummed.
我当时好沮丧。

1039
00:53:46.230 --> 00:53:46.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1040
00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:49.770
I mean, she actually is just wearing what she wore to work.
她其实穿的就是平时上班的衣服。

1041
00:53:49.930 --> 00:53:51.990
She didn't even change out of her work clothes.
她甚至连工作服都没换。

1042
00:53:52.170 --> 00:53:52.670
I know.
我知道。

1043
00:53:52.930 --> 00:53:55.250
But some of the cast did get to dress up.
但有些演员确实打扮了一番。

1044
00:53:55.410 --> 00:54:02.410
BJ, Rain, Mindy, and I'm sure our wardrobe stylist was thrilled to do something other than just drab office attire.
BJ、雷恩、敏迪，我相信我们的服装造型师一定很高兴能做些除了沉闷办公室装束以外的造型。

1045
00:54:02.670 --> 00:54:07.030
They used to get so excited every time we got to wear anything other than our office attire.
每次能穿上非办公室装束，他们都会特别兴奋。

1046
00:54:07.170 --> 00:54:11.110
And Pam didn't really dress up, but she is not in her office attire, which was fun.
帕姆虽然没怎么刻意打扮，但她穿的不是办公室装束，这很有趣。

1047
00:54:11.190 --> 00:54:12.950
I had a whole separate fitting for that.
我为此专门试了一次装。

1048
00:54:13.150 --> 00:54:14.530
We got to see casual Pam.
我们看到了休闲版的帕姆。

1049
00:54:15.190 --> 00:54:17.830
And did you notice I got to wear my hair differently as well?
你注意到我的发型也变了吗？

1050
00:54:17.930 --> 00:54:23.230
But we did find out some interesting trivia about all the other background actors who were dressed up for this festival.
不过我们确实发现了一些关于其他参与节日装扮的背景演员的有趣花絮。

1051
00:54:23.390 --> 00:54:23.630
Yes.
是的。

1052
00:54:23.810 --> 00:54:28.790
We went to Kentopedia, and he said our casting office worked with Central Casting.
我们去找了肯托百科（Kentopedia），他说我们的选角办公室和中央选角公司（Central Casting）有合作。

1053
00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:31.990
Now, Central Casting is a casting agency in Los Angeles.
中央选角公司是洛杉矶的一家选角代理机构。

1054
00:54:31.990 --> 00:54:36.670
They specialize in sort of the background actors and filling out the picture, right?
他们专门负责招募背景演员，填充画面，对吧？

1055
00:54:37.170 --> 00:54:37.310
Yeah.
没错。

1056
00:54:37.730 --> 00:54:43.110
But Central Casting reached out to a lot of the Indian community here in Los Angeles to hire those background players.
但中央选角公司联系了洛杉矶当地许多印度裔社区的人来担任这些背景演员。

1057
00:54:43.110 --> 00:54:53.010
All in all, Kent said we had 100 extras working this episode, and every single one of them brought their own very beautiful costuming for us to use.
总而言之，肯特说我们这一集有100名临时演员，他们每个人都带来了自己非常漂亮的服装供我们使用。

1058
00:54:53.010 --> 00:55:01.470
And to kind of fill out the world, Kent also hired a professional dance company to come and lead us in some of the dances.
为了让场景更丰富，肯特还聘请了一家专业舞蹈公司来带领我们跳一些舞。

1059
00:55:01.470 --> 00:55:08.490
He found a company called NDM Dance Productions, and he hired their director choreographer, Dev Mahajan.
他找到了一家叫NDM舞蹈制作的公司，并聘请了他们的导演兼编舞德夫·马哈詹（Dev Mahajan）。

1060
00:55:08.670 --> 00:55:11.070
And Dev hired eight dancers.
德夫又雇了八名舞者。

1061
00:55:11.310 --> 00:55:18.150
He choreographed, rehearsed their dance in the morning of that day four of shooting is when we shot all the dancing.
他在拍摄第四天的那天早上编排并排练了舞蹈，我们就在那天拍完了所有的舞蹈戏份。

1062
00:55:18.150 --> 00:55:24.450
And then we filmed it later in the afternoon, and all the dancers wear their own costumes as well.
然后我们在下午晚些时候进行了拍摄，所有的舞者也都穿着他们自己的服装。

1063
00:55:24.650 --> 00:55:26.550
I actually went to the website.
我其实去看了他们的网站。

1064
00:55:26.830 --> 00:55:27.710
Of course you did, lady.
你当然会去，女士。

1065
00:55:27.830 --> 00:55:29.130
You went to the dancer's website.
你去了那个舞者的网站。

1066
00:55:29.230 --> 00:55:29.850
What'd you find out?
你发现了什么？

1067
00:55:29.950 --> 00:55:31.910
They have appeared on tons of shows.
他们上过无数的节目。

1068
00:55:32.130 --> 00:55:42.130
So You Think You Can Dance, eLive Oscar coverage, Good Morning America, Superstars of Dance, and MTV's America's Best Dance Crew.
比如《舞林争霸》、《eLive》奥斯卡报道、《早安美国》、《舞蹈巨星》以及MTV的《全美最佳舞团》。

1069
00:55:42.130 --> 00:55:46.930
If you want to look them up, you can find them at ndmdance.com.
如果你想了解他们，可以去ndmdance.com看看。

1070
00:55:47.090 --> 00:55:53.270
It was super cool, and it really did end up feeling like a real party, like a real celebration.
这真的很棒，最后感觉就像一场真正的派对，一场真正的庆典。

1071
00:55:53.550 --> 00:55:54.470
It really did.
确实如此。

1072
00:55:54.470 --> 00:56:02.130
I wish my character wanted to participate more because me, Angela, that is me, would have been right out there, like, just having a great time.
我真希望我的角色能多参与一点，因为我，安吉拉，也就是我本人，当时肯定会冲上去，玩得尽兴。

1073
00:56:02.150 --> 00:56:09.430
So it was always hard in these moments to not get to be in costume and not participate and be kind of the grump on the wall, you know?
所以在这些时刻，不能穿上戏服参与其中，只能像个扫兴鬼一样站在墙边，真的很难受，你知道吗？

1074
00:56:09.430 --> 00:56:16.410
Well, I do, and we'll talk a little bit about my dancing later, but I did get to dance a little bit, and I was thrilled.
嗯，我懂，我们稍后再聊聊我的舞姿，但我确实跳了一点，我当时兴奋极了。

1075
00:56:16.710 --> 00:56:17.010
Yes.
是的。

1076
00:56:17.010 --> 00:56:17.470
Very fun.
非常有趣。

1077
00:56:17.790 --> 00:56:21.450
All right, so yeah, so there are people that got to dress up, people that didn't.
好了，所以，有些人可以打扮，有些人则不行。

1078
00:56:21.650 --> 00:56:27.070
Michael and Carol walk in with a whole different idea of what this party is.
迈克尔和卡罗尔走进来时，对这场派对有着完全不同的理解。

1079
00:56:27.290 --> 00:56:33.030
Michael has clearly told Carol that this is a costume party, so she arrives dressed as a cheerleader.
迈克尔显然告诉卡罗尔这是一场化装舞会，所以她打扮成啦啦队长来了。

1080
00:56:33.250 --> 00:56:34.790
With pom-poMs.
还拿着啦啦球。

1081
00:56:35.150 --> 00:56:36.290
With pom-poMs.
还拿着啦啦球。

1082
00:56:36.290 --> 00:56:39.630
And Michael has his old Halloween costume on.
而迈克尔穿着他那套旧的万圣节服装。

1083
00:56:39.730 --> 00:56:41.450
He has his papier-mâché head.
他戴着那个纸糊的头套。

1084
00:56:41.890 --> 00:56:44.550
We had a fan question from Melinda O'Brien.
我们收到了梅琳达·奥布莱恩的一个粉丝提问。

1085
00:56:44.810 --> 00:56:49.950
Was Michael's costume the same one from the Halloween episode, or did they have to make another one?
迈克尔的服装是万圣节那一集里的同一套吗，还是他们又做了一套？

1086
00:56:50.110 --> 00:56:52.310
Oh, no, Melinda, we save everything.
哦，不，梅琳达，我们什么都留着。

1087
00:56:52.850 --> 00:56:59.230
Everything that anyone wore or held or used or interacted with on The Office goes into a giant warehouse.
在《办公室》里任何人穿过、拿过、用过或接触过的所有东西，都会被送进一个巨大的仓库。

1088
00:56:59.230 --> 00:57:00.150
It's tagged.
它们都有标签。

1089
00:57:00.330 --> 00:57:01.770
It's almost like an evidence room.
简直就像个证物室。

1090
00:57:01.770 --> 00:57:09.190
So when they wrote that into this episode, they just went to that warehouse, and they picked up that papier-mâché head and put it right on his shoulder again.
所以当他们把这个情节写进这一集时，他们直接去了那个仓库，拿起了那个纸糊的头套，又把它放回了他的肩膀上。

1091
00:57:09.490 --> 00:57:09.950
That's right.
没错。

1092
00:57:09.950 --> 00:57:11.950
It's like the end of Raiders of the Lost Ark.
就像《夺宝奇兵》的结尾一样。

1093
00:57:12.150 --> 00:57:16.150
It's like rows and rows of boxes with dates, tags, episode names.
就像一排排贴着日期、标签和剧集名称的箱子。

1094
00:57:16.390 --> 00:57:18.030
So they went right to that box.
所以他们直接找到了那个箱子。

1095
00:57:18.170 --> 00:57:22.870
And, of course, Michael, you know, he can take the head off, and then he just looks like he's in a suit.
当然，迈克尔，你知道，他可以把头套摘下来，然后看起来就像只是穿了件西装。

1096
00:57:22.870 --> 00:57:28.610
But Carol is stuck now as a cheerleader because Michael thought this was Indian Halloween.
但卡罗尔现在被困在啦啦队长的装扮里了，因为迈克尔以为这是印度万圣节。

1097
00:57:29.570 --> 00:57:30.690
Yes, I know.
是的，我知道。

1098
00:57:30.910 --> 00:57:31.690
Poor Carol.
可怜的卡罗尔。

1099
00:57:31.930 --> 00:57:35.510
She is such a sport in this episode.
她在这一集里真是太配合了。

1100
00:57:35.530 --> 00:57:37.270
She has to endure so much.
她不得不忍受这么多。

1101
00:57:37.450 --> 00:57:40.650
And Nancy Carell just knocked it out of the park.
南希·卡瑞尔的表现简直太棒了。

1102
00:57:40.870 --> 00:57:46.010
She plays it so perfect of just sort of, like, quietly enduring this awkward evening.
她演得太完美了，那种默默忍受尴尬夜晚的感觉拿捏得恰到好处。

1103
00:57:46.890 --> 00:57:48.610
While dressed like a cheerleader.
而且还穿着啦啦队服。

1104
00:57:48.790 --> 00:57:49.030
Yeah.
没错。

1105
00:57:49.670 --> 00:57:51.630
Well, let's move over to the buffet.
好了，我们转到自助餐那边吧。

1106
00:57:53.090 --> 00:57:54.110
Angela's at the buffet.
安吉拉正在自助餐台前。

1107
00:57:54.450 --> 00:57:57.250
She asks if they have any vegetarian options.
她问有没有素食选择。

1108
00:57:58.310 --> 00:58:02.710
She doesn't even seem satisfied when she learns that everything is vegetarian.
当得知所有食物都是素食时，她看起来甚至都不怎么满意。

1109
00:58:02.950 --> 00:58:04.050
It's all vegetarian.
全都是素食。

1110
00:58:04.070 --> 00:58:05.890
She's just in full grump mode.
她完全处于一种满脸不爽的状态。

1111
00:58:05.970 --> 00:58:07.510
She's like, just give me some bread.
她就像是说，给我点面包就行了。

1112
00:58:08.050 --> 00:58:11.790
And then the guy hands her the bread with his hands.
然后那个人直接用手把面包递给了她。

1113
00:58:11.970 --> 00:58:15.510
And, Angela, you have a line here that I am fairly certain you improvised.
安吉拉，你在这里有一句台词，我相当确定是你即兴发挥的。

1114
00:58:15.690 --> 00:58:16.130
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1115
00:58:16.130 --> 00:58:20.010
I say, you used your hands as I walk away.
我说的是，我走开时说你用手拿面包。

1116
00:58:20.270 --> 00:58:25.450
And I did improvise that because the guy literally did hand it to me with his hands.
我确实是即兴发挥的，因为那个人真的是直接用手递给我的。

1117
00:58:25.610 --> 00:58:28.970
And I thought, that's not good.
我觉得这不太好。

1118
00:58:29.490 --> 00:58:31.170
You should have used some tongs.
你应该用夹子的。

1119
00:58:31.290 --> 00:58:32.170
Some tongs.
用夹子。

1120
00:58:32.190 --> 00:58:33.450
He just handed it to me with his hands.
他直接用手递给了我。

1121
00:58:33.570 --> 00:58:36.950
And so I improvised that line and it stayed in and it makes me laugh.
所以我即兴加了那句台词，结果被保留了下来，每次看都让我发笑。

1122
00:58:37.070 --> 00:58:38.810
Of course, she goes ahead and eats it.
当然，她还是直接吃了。

1123
00:58:38.930 --> 00:58:40.470
So I guess she's not too concerned.
所以我猜她其实也没那么介意。

1124
00:58:40.470 --> 00:58:44.370
But it's clearly she's just like not having a good time.
但很明显她就是玩得不开心。

1125
00:58:44.550 --> 00:58:48.410
And she's a little like grossed out because she's seeing a lot of feet.
而且她有点被恶心到了，因为她看到了很多脚。

1126
00:58:48.770 --> 00:58:51.510
And now a guy just handed her bread with his hands.
现在又有个男的直接用手递给她面包。

1127
00:58:51.670 --> 00:58:52.150
A stranger.
一个陌生人。

1128
00:58:52.430 --> 00:58:57.030
Well, in the script, it says that you take a bite and say, ugh, garlic.
剧本里写的是你咬了一口然后说，呃，大蒜味。

1129
00:58:57.030 --> 00:59:00.490
Look, we had some fan questions about the foods.
听着，我们收到了一些粉丝关于食物的问题。

1130
00:59:00.710 --> 00:59:05.610
Stacey and Rett V both wrote in to say, was any of that delicious looking buffet food real?
Stacey 和 Rett V 都写信问，自助餐里那些看起来很美味的食物是真的吗？

1131
00:59:06.030 --> 00:59:09.370
Did you get to sample some of the cuisine while filming this episode?
拍摄这一集的时候你们有尝过那些菜肴吗？

1132
00:59:09.610 --> 00:59:11.410
Guys, it was all real food.
伙计们，那全都是真食物。

1133
00:59:12.470 --> 00:59:13.570
It was all real.
全都是真的。

1134
00:59:13.750 --> 00:59:14.610
It was all delicious.
全都很美味。

1135
00:59:14.970 --> 00:59:21.110
Kent told me we hired a specialty food stylist to create the food, that it was authentically prepared.
肯特告诉我，我们雇了一位专业食品造型师来制作这些食物，都是地道烹饪的。

1136
00:59:21.110 --> 00:59:24.750
And we had it all three days of filming and we got to eat it.
拍摄的三天里我们一直都有这些食物，而且我们都能吃。

1137
00:59:24.890 --> 00:59:25.910
And I remember that.
我记得那件事。

1138
00:59:26.050 --> 00:59:26.850
It was delicious.
真的很好吃。

1139
00:59:27.250 --> 00:59:27.930
It was delicious.
真的很好吃。

1140
00:59:27.950 --> 00:59:30.750
I only got to eat the naan, but it was very good naan.
我只吃了馕，但那馕非常好吃。

1141
00:59:31.470 --> 00:59:33.270
Oh, I ate between takes.
哦，我在拍摄间隙一直在吃。

1142
00:59:33.790 --> 00:59:34.970
I just ate it.
我就是一直在吃。

1143
00:59:35.290 --> 00:59:37.610
You don't even see Pam eating it on screen.
你在屏幕上甚至都没看到帕姆在吃。

1144
00:59:37.610 --> 00:59:39.050
I was like, I will eat this.
我当时就想，我一定要吃这个。

1145
00:59:39.290 --> 00:59:44.950
Well, now we come to one of the moments in this episode that is one of my favorites, Angela.
好了，现在到了这一集中我最喜欢的时刻之一了，安吉拉。

1146
00:59:45.270 --> 00:59:48.830
This is when Ryan meets Kelly's Giggly Sisters.
就是瑞安见到凯莉那几个爱笑的姐妹的时候。

1147
00:59:49.270 --> 00:59:49.490
Yeah.
没错。

1148
00:59:50.230 --> 00:59:52.150
It's so, so cute.
太可爱了，真的太可爱了。

1149
00:59:52.330 --> 01:00:01.650
We got some fan questions from Lindsay, Bridget, and Dan, who all want to know, do you know what Kelly's sister is saying when they're talking to Ryan?
我们收到了一些来自 Lindsay、Bridget 和 Dan 的粉丝提问，他们都想知道，你知道凯莉的姐妹们在和瑞安说话时到底在说什么吗？

1150
01:00:01.850 --> 01:00:03.890
They're saying something about Zach Braff.
她们在说关于扎克·布拉夫的事。

1151
01:00:04.130 --> 01:00:04.370
Okay.
好的。

1152
01:00:04.410 --> 01:00:06.410
Here's what the three little girls say.
这是那三个小女孩说的话。

1153
01:00:06.630 --> 01:00:09.550
They say, Kelly likes Zach Braff.
她们说，凯莉喜欢扎克·布拉夫。

1154
01:00:10.290 --> 01:00:12.390
That's what they're saying in Hindi.
这就是她们用印地语说的内容。

1155
01:00:12.510 --> 01:00:13.910
And they're sort of like teasing him.
她们当时好像是在逗他。

1156
01:00:13.910 --> 01:00:15.690
They were so cute.
她们太可爱了。

1157
01:00:15.870 --> 01:00:20.330
And they were played by Tanvir Atwal, Ananya Keper, and Jaysha Patel.
她们分别由坦维尔·阿特瓦尔、阿南亚·凯珀和贾莎·帕特尔饰演。

1158
01:00:20.530 --> 01:00:26.790
Well, the little girl who plays Kelly's sister that says the Zach Braff line, that's Jaysha.
饰演凯莉妹妹、说那句扎克·布拉夫台词的小女孩，就是贾莎。

1159
01:00:26.790 --> 01:00:33.650
I found her on Instagram, and I reached out to her to ask her about what it was like to be on the show, and she wrote back.
我在Instagram上找到了她，并联系了她，询问她出演这部剧的感受，她回信了。

1160
01:00:33.650 --> 01:00:34.970
I can't wait to share.
我迫不及待想和大家分享。

1161
01:00:35.210 --> 01:00:37.630
She must be like a grown lady now.
她现在一定长成大姑娘了。

1162
01:00:37.870 --> 01:00:39.590
She is a grown woman now.
她现在确实是一位成年女性了。

1163
01:00:39.590 --> 01:00:42.970
She told me she was 13 years old when she shot this episode.
她告诉我，拍摄这一集时她才13岁。

1164
01:00:43.270 --> 01:00:46.190
She said she had not really heard about the show.
她说她当时其实没怎么听说过这部剧。

1165
01:00:46.530 --> 01:00:49.410
She was still watching Disney Channel, she said.
她说她那时还在看迪士尼频道。

1166
01:00:49.590 --> 01:01:00.910
But she said her dad took her to the audition, and she remembers walking into the casting office and just seeing tons of other kids who were all there for the same role.
但她说她爸爸带她去参加了试镜，她记得走进选角办公室时，看到一大堆孩子都在为同一个角色竞争。

1167
01:01:01.090 --> 01:01:04.770
And she said the audition was just her saying that one line in Hindi.
她说试镜内容就是让她用印地语说那一句台词。

1168
01:01:05.090 --> 01:01:07.230
And she said she didn't speak any Hindi.
她说她根本不会说印地语。

1169
01:01:07.230 --> 01:01:14.150
So her dad told her how to say it about five seconds before she went into the audition room, and then she got the part.
所以她爸爸在进试镜室前五秒钟教了她怎么说，然后她就拿到了这个角色。

1170
01:01:14.850 --> 01:01:23.430
So she said she was so excited, and I asked her what it was like to be on set, if she had any memories, and she sent back the sweetest message.
她说她当时特别兴奋。我问她片场是什么样的，有没有什么回忆，她发回了这段最暖心的留言。

1171
01:01:23.430 --> 01:01:25.130
So we're going to play it for you now.
现在我们就放给大家听听。

1172
01:01:25.630 --> 01:01:30.650
I remember Rainn Wilson walking up to me and shoving a lightsaber in my hand and yelling,
我记得雷恩·威尔森走到我面前，把一把光剑塞进我手里，大喊着：

1173
01:01:30.810 --> 01:01:31.710
Lightsaber war!
光剑大战！

1174
01:01:31.910 --> 01:01:36.830
I also remember getting to know Mindy Kaling and BJ Novak, who were so sweet to me.
我还记得认识了敏迪·卡灵和BJ·诺瓦克，他们对我特别好。

1175
01:01:37.230 --> 01:01:44.530
Meeting Mindy Kaling really meant a lot to me growing up because I didn't really see many Indian actresses in the entertainment industry at that time.
在成长过程中，能见到敏迪·卡灵对我意义重大，因为那时我在娱乐圈里几乎看不到什么印度裔女演员。

1176
01:01:44.650 --> 01:01:50.190
And I love what Mindy has done with her platform, and she is still a huge inspiration for me till this day.
我非常喜欢敏迪利用她的平台所做的一切，直到今天，她依然是我巨大的灵感来源。

1177
01:01:50.190 --> 01:01:58.910
I also remember all of the delicious Indian food on set and getting to dance all day, and I remember being so happy that I had the chance to wear my Indian clothes.
我还记得片场所有美味的印度食物，记得整天跳舞，也记得能有机会穿上我的印度服装时我有多开心。

1178
01:01:59.350 --> 01:02:00.590
Isn't that so sweet?
是不是很暖心？

1179
01:02:00.710 --> 01:02:01.690
That is wonderful.
太棒了。

1180
01:02:02.230 --> 01:02:07.190
As I listened to it, I was just smiling so big because everything about that message is lovely.
听的时候，我脸上一直挂着大大的笑容，因为那段留言里的一切都太美好了。

1181
01:02:07.330 --> 01:02:08.450
I love all of her memories.
我喜欢她所有的回忆。

1182
01:02:08.650 --> 01:02:15.090
She's absolutely right about Mindy and what Mindy has done, and she's such an inspiration to so many people.
关于敏迪和她所做的一切，她说得完全正确，敏迪确实激励了很多人。

1183
01:02:16.070 --> 01:02:17.390
Yes, yeah.
是的，没错。

1184
01:02:17.810 --> 01:02:27.270
She told me after the episode aired, she had classmates and family members reaching out that they had recorded it and taking pictures of her name in the credits.
她告诉我，剧集播出后，她的同学和家人都联系她，说他们录下了节目，还拍下了演职员表中她的名字。

1185
01:02:28.570 --> 01:02:30.570
So that was when she was 13.
那时候她才13岁。

1186
01:02:30.570 --> 01:02:31.930
She really wanted to be an actress.
她当时真的很想成为一名演员。

1187
01:02:32.130 --> 01:02:36.570
She said when she was 15, she decided she wanted to go into journalism.
她说15岁时，她决定要从事新闻行业。

1188
01:02:36.570 --> 01:02:41.850
And now, Jaysha is the morning news reporter at NBC15 in Mobile, Alabama.
而现在，贾莎是阿拉巴马州莫比尔市NBC15台的早间新闻记者。

1189
01:02:42.370 --> 01:02:48.810
She told me she has to go to bed at 4 o'clock in the afternoon because she has to be in the studio at 3.30 in the morning.
她告诉我，她必须在下午4点就上床睡觉，因为凌晨3点半就得赶到演播室。

1190
01:02:49.330 --> 01:02:56.430
I have always heard that about these morning anchors on the East Coast, that they have to get up so early.
我一直听说东海岸的这些早间新闻主播必须起得那么早。

1191
01:02:56.710 --> 01:02:58.390
That's amazing, though, Jaysha.
不过这真的很了不起，贾莎。

1192
01:02:58.630 --> 01:02:59.850
That is so cool.
太酷了。

1193
01:03:00.210 --> 01:03:01.210
Isn't that so cool?
这难道不酷吗？

1194
01:03:01.210 --> 01:03:08.130
She said all her co-workers know about her appearance on The Office and that fans will mention to her because she's Indian.
她说她的同事们都知道她出演过《办公室》，而且因为她是印度裔，粉丝们经常会提到她。

1195
01:03:08.670 --> 01:03:14.350
They'll mention the Diwali episode, and then she always, like, blows their mind when she says, oh, no, I was in it.
他们会提到排灯节那一集，然后当她说“哦不，我其实演了那一集”时，总是会让他们大吃一惊。

1196
01:03:14.730 --> 01:03:16.310
So I thought that was so sweet.
我觉得这太可爱了。

1197
01:03:16.570 --> 01:03:17.250
I was in it.
我演了那一集。

1198
01:03:17.330 --> 01:03:19.630
I say a line that offends Ryan the Temp.
我说的台词冒犯了临时工瑞安。

1199
01:03:20.550 --> 01:03:21.510
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

1200
01:03:21.790 --> 01:03:25.010
Except he doesn't quite know he's being the butt of a joke.
只不过他还没完全意识到自己成了笑话的对象。

1201
01:03:25.270 --> 01:03:25.450
Right.
没错。

1202
01:03:25.450 --> 01:03:31.070
But she said being on The Office was one of her most memorable moments of her childhood.
但她说参演《办公室》是她童年最难忘的时刻之一。

1203
01:03:31.350 --> 01:03:36.190
I also love that, you know, I'm sure Rain improvised going up to her with that lightsaber.
我也很喜欢这一点，我知道，雷恩拿着光剑走向她那段肯定是他即兴发挥的。

1204
01:03:36.470 --> 01:03:40.510
There's a bunch of deleted scenes where he's fighting with kids with lightsabers.
还有很多删减片段是他拿着光剑跟孩子们打斗的场景。

1205
01:03:41.750 --> 01:03:43.130
And it didn't make it in.
但没能放进正片里。

1206
01:03:43.230 --> 01:03:47.930
But he, Rain looked very much in his element, like that's how he bonds with children.
不过雷恩看起来真的很自在，就像那是他跟孩子们打成一片的方式一样。

1207
01:03:48.590 --> 01:03:48.930
Yes.
是的。

1208
01:03:49.190 --> 01:03:52.830
Angela, should we check in on those folks at Stanford, see how they're doing?
安吉拉，我们要不要去看看斯坦福大学那些人，看看他们怎么样了？

1209
01:03:52.830 --> 01:03:55.110
You mean the folks drinking Jägermeister?
你是说那些喝野格利口酒的人吗？

1210
01:03:55.410 --> 01:03:55.630
Yeah.
对。

1211
01:03:55.890 --> 01:03:56.590
How are they?
他们怎么样了？

1212
01:03:56.910 --> 01:03:59.110
And Angela, did you see what they ordered for dinner?
还有安吉拉，你看到他们晚餐点了什么吗？

1213
01:03:59.230 --> 01:04:01.030
Oh, Jenna, you and I know firsthand.
噢，珍娜，你我可是深有体会。

1214
01:04:01.890 --> 01:04:06.250
You do not drink a lot of alcohol and only eat sushi.
不能喝太多酒却只吃寿司。

1215
01:04:06.630 --> 01:04:08.410
Now, Angela, why do we know that firsthand?
那么，安吉拉，为什么我们对此深有体会呢？

1216
01:04:08.410 --> 01:04:11.130
We know that because at the Golden Globes?
我们知道是因为金球奖吗？

1217
01:04:11.210 --> 01:04:12.310
Was it the Golden Globes, Jenna?
是金球奖吗，珍娜？

1218
01:04:13.390 --> 01:04:17.110
Oh, lady, I was thinking of my bachelorette party that you planned for me.
噢，亲爱的，我想到的是你为我策划的单身派对。

1219
01:04:17.150 --> 01:04:19.330
Oh, well, there was the Golden Globes, but the bachelorette?
噢，好吧，确实有金球奖那次，但单身派对呢？

1220
01:04:19.550 --> 01:04:22.310
Wait, have we repeated this mistake multiple times?
等等，我们是不是多次犯过同样的错误？

1221
01:04:22.310 --> 01:04:24.870
Except the second time, I did better.
除了第二次，我表现得好多了。

1222
01:04:25.030 --> 01:04:27.430
The first time, it did not work out well for me.
第一次，结果对我来说不太好。

1223
01:04:27.550 --> 01:04:34.110
The second time, if memory serves, sorry to say this on here, but it hit your sister pretty hard.
第二次，如果我没记错的话，很抱歉在这里说出来，但你姐姐当时喝得挺惨的。

1224
01:04:35.070 --> 01:04:35.610
Yeah.
没错。

1225
01:04:36.090 --> 01:04:40.630
Guys, Angela planned a bachelorette party for me when I was getting married to Lee,
各位，我跟李结婚的时候，安吉拉为我策划了一场单身派对，

1226
01:04:40.670 --> 01:04:43.770
and she took us all out for a sushi dinner.
她带我们所有人去吃了寿司晚餐。

1227
01:04:43.770 --> 01:04:51.250
It was a fancy-schmancy sushi place in Beverly Hills that I'd never eaten at, I'd only dreamed of.
那是一家比弗利山庄的高档寿司店，我以前从没去过，只在梦里想过。

1228
01:04:51.310 --> 01:04:54.470
And I was like, can we go there for my bachelorette?
当时我就说，我们能去那儿办我的单身派对吗？

1229
01:04:54.530 --> 01:04:56.390
They were thrilled to have us.
他们很乐意接待我们。

1230
01:04:56.530 --> 01:04:57.430
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

1231
01:04:57.590 --> 01:04:59.470
All of the ladies from the office were there.
办公室里的女士们都去了。

1232
01:04:59.650 --> 01:05:01.390
All of my other friends were there.
我所有的其他朋友也都去了。

1233
01:05:01.390 --> 01:05:06.250
And afterwards, you took us to a dance club.
之后，你带我们去了一家舞厅。

1234
01:05:06.590 --> 01:05:07.270
Hold up, lady.
