01:12:29.660 --> 01:12:32.400
This is how you know you really care about someone.
这就是你如何判断自己是否真的在乎某人。

1381
01:12:32.840 --> 01:12:38.120
Your person out there, folks, is the person you want to tell everything to right after it happens.
各位，你生命中那个重要的人，就是事情发生后你最想告诉的那个人。

1382
01:12:38.400 --> 01:12:40.580
It's who you bounce everything off of.
就是那个你什么事都想找他商量的人。

1383
01:12:40.840 --> 01:12:44.580
And Pam wants to tell her person what just happened.
帕姆想把刚才发生的事告诉她那个重要的人。

1384
01:12:46.120 --> 01:12:47.620
But she runs into Angela.
但她遇到了安吉拉。

1385
01:12:47.820 --> 01:12:47.920
Oh.
噢。

1386
01:12:49.320 --> 01:12:51.060
She needs to get her shoes.
她得去拿她的鞋子。

1387
01:12:51.440 --> 01:12:54.880
And there is Angela guarding the shoes, she says.
安吉拉守着鞋子，她说。

1388
01:12:54.900 --> 01:12:57.040
Well, and eating her dry naan.
嗯，还在吃她那干巴巴的馕。

1389
01:12:57.360 --> 01:12:59.680
By the way, Angela, fan question from Rainy Greg.
顺便问一下安吉拉，这是来自雷尼·格雷格的粉丝提问。

1390
01:12:59.880 --> 01:13:00.780
Was the naan dry?
那个馕干吗？

1391
01:13:01.420 --> 01:13:01.780
No.
不干。

1392
01:13:02.300 --> 01:13:03.380
Was it actually dry?
真的干吗？

1393
01:13:03.620 --> 01:13:03.940
No, it wasn't.
不，不干。

1394
01:13:04.080 --> 01:13:05.500
It was perfectly fine.
它好得很。

1395
01:13:05.500 --> 01:13:07.740
I would say that, too.
我也会这么说。

1396
01:13:07.820 --> 01:13:08.480
I ate some of that naan.
我吃过那个馕。

1397
01:13:08.480 --> 01:13:09.000
It was wonderful.
味道好极了。

1398
01:13:09.280 --> 01:13:10.220
I was glad to have it.
我很高兴能吃到它。

1399
01:13:10.420 --> 01:13:11.560
I was probably hungry.
我当时可能饿了。

1400
01:13:12.040 --> 01:13:17.300
Well, Jen and I used to always get so tickled to have scenes together because it rarely happened.
我和珍以前总是很期待能一起演戏，因为这种机会很少。

1401
01:13:17.300 --> 01:13:19.920
And so we were really excited about this.
所以我们对此真的感到非常兴奋。

1402
01:13:20.120 --> 01:13:22.320
I loved shooting this scene with you.
我很喜欢和你拍这场戏。

1403
01:13:22.460 --> 01:13:23.700
And I love it so much.
而且我非常喜欢它。

1404
01:13:23.720 --> 01:13:25.000
I just want us to play it.
我只是想让我们把它演出来。

1405
01:13:25.140 --> 01:13:26.060
Sam, can you play it?
萨姆，你能演一下吗？

1406
01:13:27.260 --> 01:13:28.160
It's hot in there.
里面很热。

1407
01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:30.880
How's the naan?
馕怎么样？

1408
01:13:31.260 --> 01:13:31.680
Dry.
干巴巴的。

1409
01:13:32.580 --> 01:13:33.900
Looked like you were having fun.
看起来你玩得很开心。

1410
01:13:34.480 --> 01:13:35.140
I am.
我是挺开心的。

1411
01:13:35.360 --> 01:13:36.540
You should come dance with us.
你应该过来和我们一起跳舞。

1412
01:13:36.800 --> 01:13:39.060
I have to watch our shoes so they don't get stolen.
我得看着我们的鞋子，免得被偷了。

1413
01:13:39.700 --> 01:13:40.660
Who are you texting?
你在给谁发短信？

1414
01:13:41.120 --> 01:13:41.640
No one.
没给谁。

1415
01:13:42.680 --> 01:13:42.920
Aw.
噢。

1416
01:13:43.140 --> 01:13:47.340
But also, lady, my character is so nosy.
但话说回来，女士，我的角色真是太爱管闲事了。

1417
01:13:48.360 --> 01:13:49.080
So nosy?
很爱管闲事？

1418
01:13:49.160 --> 01:13:49.640
Who are you texting?
你在给谁发短信？

1419
01:13:49.660 --> 01:13:50.640
Yeah, looked like you were having fun.
是啊，看起来你玩得很开心。

1420
01:13:50.660 --> 01:13:51.260
Who are you texting?
你在给谁发短信？

1421
01:13:51.460 --> 01:13:54.300
I mean, who am I to ask you who you're texting?
我是说，我算老几啊，竟然问你在给谁发短信？

1422
01:13:55.360 --> 01:13:56.700
You're the party police.
你是派对纠察员。

1423
01:13:56.700 --> 01:13:58.460
Also, you're single.
再说，你还是单身。

1424
01:13:58.820 --> 01:14:01.080
Dwight made this big announcement that he's single.
德怀特大张旗鼓地宣布他单身。

1425
01:14:01.320 --> 01:14:02.040
I don't know.
我不知道。

1426
01:14:02.200 --> 01:14:03.300
Maybe you're texting Dwight.
也许你在给德怀特发短信。

1427
01:14:03.480 --> 01:14:04.000
What's happening?
发生了什么事？

1428
01:14:04.480 --> 01:14:05.960
Angela's spinning out in this episode.
安吉拉在这一集里情绪失控了。

1429
01:14:06.180 --> 01:14:08.120
And a lot of those scenes ended up getting deleted.
而且很多那样的场景最终都被删掉了。

1430
01:14:08.120 --> 01:14:14.220
But it would be a fun watch to go back and watch them because that is why you are so intense in this episode.
但回头去看看那些片段会很有趣，因为那就是你在这一集里表现得那么紧张的原因。

1431
01:14:14.660 --> 01:14:17.780
So now Pam is going to make it outside.
所以现在帕姆要到外面去了。

1432
01:14:18.080 --> 01:14:20.960
She hasn't received a text back from Jim.
她还没有收到吉姆的回信。

1433
01:14:21.400 --> 01:14:23.180
And she sits with Michael.
然后她和迈克尔坐在一起。

1434
01:14:23.980 --> 01:14:25.520
Michael tries to relate to her.
迈克尔试图和她产生共鸣。

1435
01:14:25.520 --> 01:14:28.320
He's like, wow, they're both victims of broken engagements.
他觉得，哇，他们俩都是订婚破裂的受害者。

1436
01:14:28.820 --> 01:14:34.320
And Pam's like, well, I mean, except that you were never actually engaged, but whatever.
帕姆心想，好吧，我是说，除了你其实根本没订过婚之外，随你怎么说吧。

1437
01:14:34.600 --> 01:14:36.300
She tries to bond with Michael.
她试图和迈克尔拉近关系。

1438
01:14:36.300 --> 01:14:43.000
And, of course, he does that thing that you were just talking about where he just takes it one step too far.
当然，他做了你刚才提到的那种事，就是把事情做得太过火了。

1439
01:14:43.280 --> 01:14:46.980
And he starts to lean in like he's going to kiss her.
他开始凑过去，好像要吻她一样。

1440
01:14:47.240 --> 01:14:48.360
So awkward.
太尴尬了。

1441
01:14:48.360 --> 01:14:50.880
We got a lot of mail about it, Angela.
我们收到了很多关于此事的来信，安吉拉。

1442
01:14:51.440 --> 01:15:00.020
Ruby, Alexandra, and Vanessa Ortiz all wrote in to ask if that was a scripted moment when Michael tries to kiss Pam.
鲁比、亚历山德拉和凡妮莎·奥尔蒂斯都写信来问，迈克尔试图亲吻帕姆那一幕是不是剧本里写的。

1443
01:15:00.020 --> 01:15:02.420
Pam, what was it like?
帕姆，当时是什么感觉？

1444
01:15:02.700 --> 01:15:04.520
It was scripted, you guys.
那是剧本写的，各位。

1445
01:15:04.720 --> 01:15:05.920
That was in the script.
那是剧本里的内容。

1446
01:15:06.000 --> 01:15:12.360
And then the thing, that great line that Pam has where she says, I'm rejecting your kiss.
还有那件事，帕姆那句精彩的台词，她说：我拒绝你的吻。

1447
01:15:12.500 --> 01:15:14.040
He's like, she's like, what are you doing?
他问，她问，你在干什么？

1448
01:15:14.100 --> 01:15:14.820
He's like, what are you doing?
他问，你在干什么？

1449
01:15:14.920 --> 01:15:16.820
She's like, I'm rejecting your kiss.
她说，我拒绝你的吻。

1450
01:15:16.980 --> 01:15:17.940
That's what I'm doing.
我就是在做这个。

1451
01:15:17.940 --> 01:15:20.120
Yeah, what are you doing?
没错，你在干什么？

1452
01:15:20.360 --> 01:15:21.840
That was all scripted.
那都是写好的剧本。

1453
01:15:21.960 --> 01:15:29.620
And, Angela, I was so excited to do that scene because I remember staying late that evening and shooting outside.
而且，安吉拉，我当时拍那场戏特别兴奋，因为我记得那天晚上我们留得很晚，在外面拍摄。

1454
01:15:30.040 --> 01:15:37.440
I talked about this before when I had that scene with John up on the roof where Pam and Jim eat the grilled cheese sandwiches.
我之前提到过，就是我和约翰在屋顶上拍的那场戏，帕姆和吉姆在那儿吃烤奶酪三明治。

1455
01:15:37.440 --> 01:15:41.080
It was one of those warm summer evenings in Los Angeles.
那是洛杉矶一个温暖的夏夜。

1456
01:15:41.080 --> 01:15:42.040
They're the beSt.
它们是最棒的。

1457
01:15:42.380 --> 01:15:44.200
This was another one of those.
这又是其中之一。

1458
01:15:44.200 --> 01:15:53.420
And it's one of my fondest memories from shooting the show because I got Steve all to myself, and I got Miguel Arteta all to myself, and Mindy was there,
这是我拍摄这部剧时最美好的回忆之一，因为我能独享史蒂夫，还能独享米格尔·阿特塔，明迪也在场，

1459
01:15:53.560 --> 01:15:57.860
and it was just us doing this scene, getting it just perfect.
当时就我们几个人在拍这场戏，力求完美。

1460
01:15:57.860 --> 01:16:00.000
It felt like we had all the time in the world.
感觉我们有的是时间。

1461
01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:01.240
There was no rush.
一点也不赶。

1462
01:16:01.600 --> 01:16:04.520
And, oh, I just absolutely loved it.
噢，我真的太喜欢了。

1463
01:16:04.820 --> 01:16:12.920
Yeah, well, Mindy mentioned, you know, that she was kind of jealous of her parents that they got to have this great scene with Steve because there are several characters,
是啊，明迪提到过，你知道，她其实有点嫉妒她父母能和史蒂夫演这场精彩的戏，因为有很多角色，

1464
01:16:13.160 --> 01:16:13.820
myself included,
包括我在内，

1465
01:16:13.820 --> 01:16:16.720
that rarely got to have one-on-one scenes with Steve.
都很少有机会和史蒂夫演对手戏。

1466
01:16:16.880 --> 01:16:19.000
It just wouldn't make sense in the world of the show.
在剧中的世界观里，这确实说不通。

1467
01:16:19.180 --> 01:16:22.660
And whenever I did, it felt so special.
所以每当我能和他演对手戏时，都觉得特别珍贵。

1468
01:16:22.880 --> 01:16:28.140
And I think you got to have some amazing scenes with him throughout the course of the show,
我觉得你在整部剧里和他演过不少精彩的戏，

1469
01:16:28.140 --> 01:16:36.020
and this is just one of those that was just beautiful and so fun and funny and cringy and heartfelt, just all of it.
而这一场既美妙又有趣，既好笑又尴尬，还很感人，应有尽有。

1470
01:16:36.140 --> 01:16:36.760
That's all true.
确实如此。

1471
01:16:36.940 --> 01:16:41.600
Angela, we did have someone write in with an old tech alert that I thought you would appreciate.
安吉拉，有位观众发来了一条关于老式科技的提醒，我想你会感兴趣的。

1472
01:16:41.600 --> 01:16:42.160
Hit me up.
说来听听。

1473
01:16:42.200 --> 01:16:42.900
How did I miss it?
我怎么错过了？

1474
01:16:42.900 --> 01:16:43.440
What is it?
是什么？

1475
01:16:43.580 --> 01:16:53.260
Kayla Whitehead said Pam's cell phone is such old tech, but she's like, but also, when she walks outside, Michael sees her on the steps,
凯拉·怀特黑德说帕姆的手机真是老古董了，但她说，还有，当她走到外面时，迈克尔在台阶上看到了她，

1476
01:16:53.260 --> 01:16:57.320
and he notices that she's holding her phone, and he says, expecting a call.
他注意到她拿着手机，然后他说，在等电话吗。

1477
01:16:57.760 --> 01:17:00.240
She was like, no one would say that to you today.
她说，现在没人会那样跟你说话了。

1478
01:17:00.300 --> 01:17:06.400
If you have your phone in your hand today, no one's, like, expecting a call because we always all have our phones in our hands.
如果你现在手里拿着手机，没人会问你是不是在等电话，因为我们现在手机总是拿在手里。

1479
01:17:06.520 --> 01:17:08.620
That is a brilliant catch.
这观察太敏锐了。

1480
01:17:08.680 --> 01:17:11.060
I am applauding that catch.
我为这个发现鼓掌。

1481
01:17:11.060 --> 01:17:12.640
I love that observation.
我喜欢这个观察。

1482
01:17:13.000 --> 01:17:16.920
That is an amazing observation because back then, yeah, your phone was in your purse.
这观察太棒了，因为那时候，没错，手机都是放在包里的。

1483
01:17:17.080 --> 01:17:22.960
It was, we didn't walk around holding phones, like flip phones like that, because we did hardly anything with them other than talk to someone.
确实，我们不会像那样拿着翻盖手机到处走，因为除了打电话，我们几乎不用手机做别的事。

1484
01:17:23.000 --> 01:17:26.520
So if you're holding it, you'd probably just spoke to someone or you were about to.
所以如果你拿着手机，你可能刚打完电话，或者正准备打。

1485
01:17:26.520 --> 01:17:28.580
Yes, that is a great observation.
没错，这观察太棒了。

1486
01:17:28.800 --> 01:17:29.020
Pretty great.
相当棒。

1487
01:17:29.020 --> 01:17:39.420
Well, I want to take us back to Stanford because I think there is a moment in this episode that is the happiest we have seen Andy since he has appeared on the show.
我想带大家回到斯坦福，因为我觉得这一集中有一个时刻，是安迪自出场以来最开心的时候。

1488
01:17:39.860 --> 01:17:41.220
It's Happy Andy.
那是开心的安迪。

1489
01:17:41.640 --> 01:17:45.240
And I want to talk, I want to share Happy Andy with you.
我想聊聊，我想和你们分享开心的安迪。

1490
01:17:45.920 --> 01:17:48.260
Happy Andy happens at around 15 minutes.
开心的安迪出现在大约15分钟的时候。

1491
01:17:48.260 --> 01:17:51.140
It's, they have had a lot of Jaeger.
他们喝了很多野格酒。

1492
01:17:51.640 --> 01:17:55.700
Karen, though, she's just tossing her Jaeger shots into the trash.
不过凯伦把她的野格酒都倒进垃圾桶了。

1493
01:17:55.980 --> 01:17:57.160
No one knows it.
没人发现。

1494
01:17:57.440 --> 01:17:58.920
She's not getting wasted.
她没喝醉。

1495
01:17:59.680 --> 01:18:02.380
And Andy starts singing acapella.
然后安迪开始唱阿卡贝拉。

1496
01:18:02.540 --> 01:18:04.120
Karen's like, no acapella, Andy.
凯伦说，别唱阿卡贝拉，安迪。

1497
01:18:04.300 --> 01:18:08.280
But he's drunk and he's singing the Indigo Girls Closer to Fine.
但他喝醉了，还在唱Indigo Girls的《Closer to Fine》。

1498
01:18:08.280 --> 01:18:15.220
And as he drunkenly sings, all of a sudden, Jim, who's super wasted, starts joining in and singing.
当他醉醺醺地唱着时，突然，喝得烂醉的吉姆也加入进来一起唱。

1499
01:18:15.480 --> 01:18:18.020
And it's so adorable.
太可爱了。

1500
01:18:18.280 --> 01:18:19.760
Andy's like, Tuna!
安迪说，金枪鱼！

1501
01:18:19.760 --> 01:18:21.340
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1502
01:18:21.540 --> 01:18:24.860
Like, he's so happy.
你看，他好开心。

1503
01:18:25.140 --> 01:18:26.100
He's so happy.
他真的好开心。

1504
01:18:26.240 --> 01:18:28.100
They're having like an acapella moment.
他们好像在进行一场无伴奏合唱。

1505
01:18:28.300 --> 01:18:30.280
And this is Happy Andy.
这就是开心的安迪。

1506
01:18:30.500 --> 01:18:31.300
He is thrilled.
他激动坏了。

1507
01:18:31.600 --> 01:18:36.340
Well, Angela, we had a fan catch from Renata Torres.
安吉拉，我们收到了一位粉丝蕾娜塔·托雷斯的发现。

1508
01:18:36.920 --> 01:18:44.280
She says at 17 minutes, 58 seconds, you can see a pair of white flip-flops under Karen's desk.
她说在17分58秒的时候，你可以看到凯伦桌子底下有一双白色人字拖。

1509
01:18:44.340 --> 01:18:44.620
Ah!
啊！

1510
01:18:45.100 --> 01:18:49.140
And she wanted to know if that was on purpose, but we know why those are there.
她想知道那是故意的吗，但我们知道那是怎么回事。

1511
01:18:49.400 --> 01:18:50.060
We do.
没错。

1512
01:18:50.240 --> 01:18:51.760
Those were Rashida's flip-flops.
那是拉什达的人字拖。

1513
01:18:51.980 --> 01:18:59.360
Yeah, the wardrobe department would give us Uggs or flip-flops to wear to and from our trailers and set
对，服装组会给我们UGG雪地靴或人字拖，让我们在拖车和片场之间穿，

1514
01:18:59.360 --> 01:19:04.020
so we didn't have to walk in our kind of like high-heel office shoes, right?
这样我们就不用穿着那种高跟办公鞋走来走去了，对吧？

1515
01:19:04.160 --> 01:19:04.480
Yes.
是的。

1516
01:19:05.200 --> 01:19:05.640
Yes!
没错！

1517
01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:08.880
You caught Rashida's flip-flops.
你发现了拉什达的人字拖。

1518
01:19:09.100 --> 01:19:15.040
You know, wardrobe actually told me one time also, our trailers were not close to the soundstage.
你知道吗，服装组有次还告诉我，我们的拖车离摄影棚并不近。

1519
01:19:15.160 --> 01:19:16.720
It was a little, you know, quite a walk.
那段路其实挺远的。

1520
01:19:16.860 --> 01:19:20.540
And they said that also they would take our shoes to protect our shoes.
他们说这样做也是为了保护我们的鞋子。

1521
01:19:20.760 --> 01:19:26.060
Because if we walked across the parking lot back and forth, and sometimes if there was weather of any kind,
因为如果我们穿着它们在停车场走来走去，万一遇到什么恶劣天气，

1522
01:19:26.060 --> 01:19:34.080
they preferred actually to leave our shoes on set by our desks rather than us walking around in them all the time.
他们更倾向于把我们的鞋子留在片场的办公桌旁，而不是让我们一直穿着走动。

1523
01:19:34.220 --> 01:19:36.580
And we were delighted because that meant less time in heels.
我们当时很高兴，因为这意味着少穿高跟鞋的时间。

1524
01:19:36.580 --> 01:19:38.160
We had our travel shoes.
我们有我们的通勤鞋。

1525
01:19:38.380 --> 01:19:40.400
Those were Rashida's travel shoes.
那是拉什达的通勤鞋。

1526
01:19:40.960 --> 01:19:46.960
Well, as they're leaving for the night in Stanford, Jim is going to ride that bike home.
好了，当他们在斯坦福准备下班时，吉姆打算骑那辆自行车回家。

1527
01:19:47.140 --> 01:19:48.720
He's going to ride his bike home.
他打算骑车回家。

1528
01:19:48.840 --> 01:19:49.820
Or is he?
真的是这样吗？

1529
01:19:49.900 --> 01:19:50.480
Well, yeah.
嗯，是的。

1530
01:19:50.700 --> 01:19:51.680
He falls over.
他摔倒了。

1531
01:19:51.680 --> 01:19:53.960
Well, you know, it's the end of the night at Stanford.
好吧，你知道，那是斯坦福之夜的结束。

1532
01:19:53.980 --> 01:19:54.940
They've had Jaeger.
他们喝了野格酒。

1533
01:19:55.200 --> 01:19:56.960
They've bonded over Indigo Girls.
他们因为Indigo Girls乐队的歌而建立了感情。

1534
01:19:57.540 --> 01:20:00.080
I mean, Andy's busting out his air mattress.
我是说，安迪都要把他的充气床垫拿出来了。

1535
01:20:00.420 --> 01:20:01.220
He's like...
他就像是……

1536
01:20:01.220 --> 01:20:01.680
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1537
01:20:01.920 --> 01:20:03.580
He's staying in for the night.
他打算在那儿过夜。

1538
01:20:04.120 --> 01:20:08.120
Jim is going to try to ride his giant bicycle with the big basket home.
吉姆打算骑着他那辆带大篮子的巨型自行车回家。

1539
01:20:08.120 --> 01:20:11.140
And he, like, tips over into the bushes.
然后他就像那样，一头栽进了灌木丛里。

1540
01:20:11.140 --> 01:20:13.460
And Karen's in her car.
而凯伦正在她的车里。

1541
01:20:13.460 --> 01:20:14.620
She's like, hold up.
她就像是，等等。

1542
01:20:14.780 --> 01:20:16.240
Get in my car, drunky.
上我的车吧，醉鬼。

1543
01:20:16.940 --> 01:20:21.020
And, Jenna, do you remember how freaked out people were about this moment?
而且，珍娜，你还记得大家对这一幕有多抓狂吗？

1544
01:20:22.380 --> 01:20:22.820
Yeah.
记得。

1545
01:20:23.040 --> 01:20:28.420
I mean, people thought Karen was shady, that she let them get so wasted, and that...
我是说，人们觉得凯伦很阴险，觉得她故意让他们喝得烂醉，而且……

1546
01:20:28.420 --> 01:20:30.240
Was she waiting for Jim?
她是专门在等吉姆吗？

1547
01:20:30.240 --> 01:20:31.660
Like she had planned it all along.
就好像这一切都是她预谋好的一样。

1548
01:20:31.660 --> 01:20:33.840
Yeah, was she waiting out in the parking lot for Jim?
对，她是在停车场等吉姆吗？

1549
01:20:33.840 --> 01:20:36.140
I was like, hey, Mr. Tipsy, get in my car.
我就像是，嘿，醉醺醺的先生，上我的车吧。

1550
01:20:36.140 --> 01:20:41.180
And remember, in this episode, it was written that they were going to, like, kiss.
而且要记住，在这一集中，剧本里写着他们本来是要接吻的。

1551
01:20:41.580 --> 01:20:43.020
Oh, I talked to Rashida about it.
哦，我和拉什达聊过这件事。

1552
01:20:43.080 --> 01:20:46.720
I texted with her, and I want to read you guys what she said.
我跟她发了短信，想读给你们听听她是怎么说的。

1553
01:20:46.880 --> 01:20:53.580
She said, in this episode, they had written a scene where Jim and Karen get sloppy drunk and make out.
她说，在这一集里，剧本原本写了一场戏，吉姆和凯伦喝得烂醉如泥，然后亲热起来。

1554
01:20:53.760 --> 01:20:57.760
So maybe, I guess, she had been drinking, too, in that different version, right?
所以我想，在那个版本里，她可能也喝多了，对吧？

1555
01:20:58.240 --> 01:21:02.220
In that different version, because I have the scripted version of that,
在那个不同的版本里，因为我有那一版的剧本，

1556
01:21:02.220 --> 01:21:07.160
that they, the three of them go to a bar, and they all get drunk together at a bar.
他们三个人去了酒吧，在酒吧里一起喝醉了。

1557
01:21:07.380 --> 01:21:11.260
And then they were supposed to make out on the street outside of this bar.
然后他们本该在酒吧外面的街上亲热。

1558
01:21:11.440 --> 01:21:11.540
Yeah.
没错。

1559
01:21:11.960 --> 01:21:16.760
And Rashida said they actually filmed the scene in the parking lot.
拉什达说他们实际上在停车场拍了那场戏。

1560
01:21:17.820 --> 01:21:18.520
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1561
01:21:18.800 --> 01:21:21.080
And she said she was really worried.
她说她当时真的很担心。

1562
01:21:21.240 --> 01:21:22.380
She was like, everyone's going to hate me.
她觉得，大家都会讨厌我的。

1563
01:21:22.380 --> 01:21:27.640
And then she told me Stephen Merchant actually suggested that they cut the scene out.
后来她告诉我，其实是斯蒂芬·莫昌特建议把那场戏删掉的。

1564
01:21:28.420 --> 01:21:29.960
That he got to watch a verse.
因为他看了样片。

1565
01:21:30.060 --> 01:21:34.960
Because Stephen and Ricky would watch our episodes, and they would give the producers notes.
斯蒂芬和瑞奇会看我们的剧集，并给制片人提意见。

1566
01:21:35.580 --> 01:21:36.820
Rarely, but sometimes.
虽然很少，但偶尔会提。

1567
01:21:37.080 --> 01:21:39.360
And their notes were always correct.
而且他们的意见总是很准确。

1568
01:21:39.700 --> 01:21:42.980
They were always like, they knew, don't move that needle so far.
他们总是很清楚，知道不能把尺度拉得太开。

1569
01:21:42.980 --> 01:21:47.240
Yeah, and Rashida said she felt like Stephen really understood the relationships.
没错，拉什达说她觉得斯蒂芬真的很懂这些人物关系。

1570
01:21:47.960 --> 01:21:51.260
And that this was going too far, too bold, too quickly.
他认为那样做太过了，太突兀，也太快了。

1571
01:21:51.660 --> 01:21:55.120
And it would sort of sabotage anything that Jim and Karen might,
那会破坏掉吉姆和凯伦之间可能产生的任何火花，

1572
01:21:55.500 --> 01:21:57.720
could possibly be as a foil for Pam.
以及他们作为帕姆的对照组所能起到的作用。

1573
01:21:57.860 --> 01:21:58.740
It was just too much.
那真的太过火了。

1574
01:21:58.940 --> 01:22:03.580
Yeah, I think if you wanted to believe in their relationship, which you will,
是啊，我觉得如果你想相信他们的感情，而你确实会相信的，

1575
01:22:03.980 --> 01:22:07.200
like Jim and Karen are going to really have a great relationship.
因为吉姆和凯伦确实会有一段很棒的感情。

1576
01:22:07.380 --> 01:22:11.340
You don't want it to start off with like a sloppy drunk make out.
你肯定不希望这段感情是以那种烂醉如泥的亲热开始的。

1577
01:22:11.340 --> 01:22:12.820
On the side of the street.
就在路边。

1578
01:22:13.160 --> 01:22:13.960
Kids, are you listening?
孩子们，你们在听吗？

1579
01:22:14.140 --> 01:22:15.560
Nothing good happens after midnight.
午夜之后没好事。

1580
01:22:15.880 --> 01:22:16.760
Okay, go home.
好了，回家吧。

1581
01:22:17.140 --> 01:22:19.000
This is what my aunt told me when I went off to college.
这是我上大学时我姑妈告诉我的。

1582
01:22:19.240 --> 01:22:23.020
She said, here's my advice to you about sleeping around.
她说，关于私生活，我给你个建议。

1583
01:22:23.300 --> 01:22:24.380
This is what she said.
她是这么说的。

1584
01:22:24.800 --> 01:22:26.720
She said, you're going to go to these parties.
她说，你会去参加各种派对。

1585
01:22:27.140 --> 01:22:28.460
You're going to do some drinking.
你会喝点酒。

1586
01:22:28.840 --> 01:22:32.800
And you might, in the moment, want to make a decision that's impulsive.
在那一刻，你可能会想做一个冲动的决定。

1587
01:22:33.140 --> 01:22:35.660
She said, my advice to you is go home.
她说，我的建议是回家。

1588
01:22:36.280 --> 01:22:39.160
Because you can always wake up in the morning and say,
因为你总可以在第二天早上醒来时说，

1589
01:22:39.280 --> 01:22:41.060
oh, I wish I'd slept with that guy.
哦，我真希望昨晚和那个人睡了。

1590
01:22:41.340 --> 01:22:43.100
And you can do something about it.
到时候你还可以补救。

1591
01:22:43.360 --> 01:22:44.800
But you can't undo.
但你无法撤销。

1592
01:22:45.220 --> 01:22:46.320
You can't undo.
你无法撤销。

1593
01:22:47.160 --> 01:22:48.600
Yeah, I'm with your aunt.
没错，我支持你姑妈的观点。

1594
01:22:48.860 --> 01:22:50.040
You can't undo.
你无法撤销。

1595
01:22:50.340 --> 01:22:52.240
But I was kind of lame in college.
不过我上大学时挺无趣的。

1596
01:22:52.460 --> 01:22:58.820
When I turned 21, I had a big paper due for a class I was taking.
我21岁生日那天，有一门课要交一篇大论文。

1597
01:22:59.920 --> 01:23:01.920
And all my friends were like, you're going to go out.
我所有的朋友都说，你得出去玩啊。

1598
01:23:02.080 --> 01:23:02.880
It's your 21st birthday.
今天是你的21岁生日。

1599
01:23:03.300 --> 01:23:05.500
And I said, oh, no, I need to work on my paper.
我说，哦，不，我得写论文。

1600
01:23:05.500 --> 01:23:06.800
So I worked on my paper.
于是我就去写论文了。

1601
01:23:07.000 --> 01:23:09.700
And my dad had a Texaco gas card.
我爸当时有一张德士古加油卡。

1602
01:23:09.700 --> 01:23:11.960
And he would pay my Texaco gas card.
他会帮我付德士古加油卡的账单。

1603
01:23:12.480 --> 01:23:15.680
Just like Reality Bites, I would go to that gas station.
就像电影《四个毕业生》里那样，我会去那个加油站。

1604
01:23:15.720 --> 01:23:21.000
And I would get gas, bread, sandwich, meat, potato chips, soda, like everything.
我会去加油，买面包、三明治、肉、薯片、汽水，什么都买。

1605
01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:24.260
And I went to Texaco.
我去了德士古。

1606
01:23:24.260 --> 01:23:27.040
And I bought myself a Coronita.
我还给自己买了一瓶小科罗娜啤酒。

1607
01:23:27.680 --> 01:23:29.420
It's not even the big Corona.
甚至都不是大瓶的科罗娜。

1608
01:23:29.700 --> 01:23:30.940
It's a Coronita.
就是一瓶小科罗娜。

1609
01:23:31.580 --> 01:23:32.980
Because I was 21.
因为我当时21岁。

1610
01:23:33.400 --> 01:23:35.840
And I went and I worked on my term paper.
然后我去写我的学期论文了。

1611
01:23:35.980 --> 01:23:37.320
And I had my Coronita.
我就喝着我的小科罗娜。

1612
01:23:37.480 --> 01:23:39.040
And that was my 21st birthday.
那就是我的21岁生日。

1613
01:23:39.980 --> 01:23:41.380
That is literally adorable.
这简直太可爱了。

1614
01:23:43.020 --> 01:23:43.860
That is adorable.
太可爱了。

1615
01:23:44.060 --> 01:23:45.080
I was a big dork lady.
我以前是个大书呆子。

1616
01:23:45.280 --> 01:23:46.360
That's why we would have been friends.
这就是为什么我们本来会成为朋友。

1617
01:23:46.440 --> 01:23:48.160
I would have hung out with you and your cat.
我本来会和你还有你的猫一起玩。

1618
01:23:48.380 --> 01:23:49.320
We would have been besties.
我们本来会成为闺蜜的。

1619
01:23:50.060 --> 01:23:55.100
This is also why, as adults, we mixed sushi with a lot of hard liquor.
这也是为什么我们成年后，会把寿司和大量烈酒混在一起吃。

1620
01:23:55.180 --> 01:23:56.740
Because we didn't learn in college.
因为我们在大学里没学乖。

1621
01:23:56.740 --> 01:23:57.480
We didn't learn.
我们没学乖。

1622
01:23:57.600 --> 01:23:58.260
Where are we at?
我们讲到哪儿了？

1623
01:23:58.260 --> 01:23:59.460
I don't even know where we're at.
我甚至都不知道我们讲到哪儿了。

1624
01:23:59.500 --> 01:24:01.260
Except that Karen put Jim in his car.
只知道凯伦把吉姆送上了车。

1625
01:24:01.520 --> 01:24:03.240
And now we go back to Diwali.
现在我们回到排灯节那一集。

1626
01:24:03.440 --> 01:24:05.300
And it's one of my favorite moments ever.
那是我最喜欢的时刻之一。

1627
01:24:05.940 --> 01:24:10.540
Dwight and Michael are going to perform a cover of Adam Sandler's Hanukkah song.
德怀特和迈克尔要表演亚当·桑德勒的《光明节之歌》翻唱版。

1628
01:24:11.400 --> 01:24:13.120
Dedicated to Indians everywhere.
献给全世界的印度人。

1629
01:24:14.360 --> 01:24:16.300
Yes, the crowd loves it.
没错，观众很喜欢。

1630
01:24:16.740 --> 01:24:20.260
Angela, so many people wrote in asking about this song.
安吉拉，好多人写信来问这首歌的事。

1631
01:24:20.400 --> 01:24:21.440
Was it improvised?
它是即兴创作的吗？

1632
01:24:21.660 --> 01:24:26.680
A lot of people thought that because Steve was holding a piece of paper that maybe we wrote this on the fly.
很多人都这么想，因为史蒂夫手里拿着一张纸，以为我们是临时写的。

1633
01:24:27.000 --> 01:24:29.360
No, this was in the script.
不，这是剧本里写好的。

1634
01:24:29.360 --> 01:24:35.440
And in fact, Kent told me it had been in the script as far back as the pre-table draft.
事实上，肯特告诉我，早在剧本围读前的草稿里就有这一段了。

1635
01:24:35.800 --> 01:24:37.520
This is kind of a writer's term.
这算是个编剧术语。

1636
01:24:37.660 --> 01:24:41.400
But they send out a draft of the script before they let anyone see it.
他们在给任何人看之前，会先发出一份剧本草稿。

1637
01:24:41.480 --> 01:24:47.740
And they have to give it to all of the main producers so that they can start planning wardrobe and locations.
他们必须把它交给所有的主要制片人，这样他们才能开始规划服装和拍摄地点。

1638
01:24:48.160 --> 01:24:53.060
And Kent said that at that pre-table draft, this was the tag for the episode.
肯特说在那个围读前草稿里，这就是这一集的结尾彩蛋。

1639
01:24:53.060 --> 01:24:55.680
And it remained there until we shot it.
直到拍摄时它都一直保留着。

1640
01:24:55.680 --> 01:24:58.520
So they got permission and all that kind of stuff.
所以他们获得了版权许可之类的东西。

1641
01:24:58.680 --> 01:25:05.580
And he said Steve asked for that piece of paper because he felt like his character wrote it at the party.
他说史蒂夫要那张纸是因为他觉得他的角色是在派对上现写的。

1642
01:25:05.780 --> 01:25:10.500
And that would sell the idea that this was like a last-minute idea by Michael.
这样更能让人相信这是迈克尔临时起意想出来的。

1643
01:25:10.680 --> 01:25:11.060
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1644
01:25:11.180 --> 01:25:12.060
I thought the same thing.
我也这么想。

1645
01:25:12.220 --> 01:25:14.620
I thought Michael needed those notes.
我以为迈克尔需要那些笔记。

1646
01:25:14.780 --> 01:25:15.560
Steve did not.
史蒂夫其实不需要。

1647
01:25:16.440 --> 01:25:16.720
Right.
没错。

1648
01:25:17.240 --> 01:25:17.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1649
01:25:17.760 --> 01:25:19.020
Well, it's so good.
嗯，这真的太棒了。

1650
01:25:19.020 --> 01:25:21.480
And I have a really great catch.
我还有一个很棒的发现。

1651
01:25:21.660 --> 01:25:23.940
I'm going to call it a BFF catch.
我要把它称为“闺蜜捕捉瞬间”。

1652
01:25:24.620 --> 01:25:25.680
What is it?
那是什么？

1653
01:25:25.800 --> 01:25:32.520
At 20 minutes, 34 seconds, after he's finished singing and it pans to the crowd and everyone cheers,
在20分34秒的时候，他唱完歌，镜头扫向人群，大家都在欢呼，

1654
01:25:33.060 --> 01:25:35.980
you and I are sitting side by side on the floor together.
你和我正并排坐在地板上。

1655
01:25:36.860 --> 01:25:38.640
Oh, my gosh, Angela.
天哪，安吉拉。

1656
01:25:38.900 --> 01:25:40.900
You know we did that ourselves.
你知道那是我们自己坐那儿的。

1657
01:25:40.900 --> 01:25:41.580
I know.
我知道。

1658
01:25:41.820 --> 01:25:42.620
We sat together.
我们坐在一起。

1659
01:25:42.840 --> 01:25:43.480
We probably were.
我们可能确实坐在一起。

1660
01:25:43.640 --> 01:25:45.680
I mean, I remember them doing that song.
我是说，我记得他们唱那首歌的时候。

1661
01:25:45.680 --> 01:25:48.400
We were all just elated and along for the ride.
我们当时都沉浸在那种兴奋和快乐中。

1662
01:25:48.400 --> 01:25:49.480
It was so fun.
太有趣了。

1663
01:25:49.820 --> 01:25:54.720
And I think we just sat next to each other because they probably weren't even sure if they were going
我想我们只是刚好坐在彼此旁边，因为他们可能甚至不确定是否会

1664
01:25:54.720 --> 01:25:57.300
to use that big swing back to the crowd, right?
用到那个扫向人群的大摇臂镜头，对吧？

1665
01:25:57.800 --> 01:25:58.280
Yeah.
没错。

1666
01:25:58.600 --> 01:25:59.800
And so there we are.
所以我们就出现在那儿了。

1667
01:25:59.840 --> 01:26:01.460
There we are on the ground next to each other.
我们就那样坐在地上，挨在一起。

1668
01:26:01.660 --> 01:26:02.540
BFF catch.
闺蜜捕捉瞬间。

1669
01:26:03.500 --> 01:26:08.140
That is the perfect way to end this podcast episode of Diwali.
这真是结束这期《排灯节》播客的最佳方式。

1670
01:26:08.380 --> 01:26:10.140
We did it with a BFF catch.
我们以一个“闺蜜捕捉瞬间”结束了。

1671
01:26:10.240 --> 01:26:10.800
We did it.
我们做到了。

1672
01:26:10.900 --> 01:26:14.560
And thank you so much to Mindy Kaling for stopping by.
非常感谢敏迪·卡灵（Mindy Kaling）的到来。

1673
01:26:15.200 --> 01:26:19.380
I just felt like we could kept talking and talking and I can't wait for her to come back.
我觉得我们还能一直聊下去，我迫不及待想让她再来。

1674
01:26:19.560 --> 01:26:24.100
And if you guys get a chance, go check out Mindy's new show that she co-created with Lang
如果大家有机会，一定要去看看敏迪和兰·费舍尔（Lang Fisher）

1675
01:26:24.100 --> 01:26:24.420
Fisher.
共同创作的新剧。

1676
01:26:24.540 --> 01:26:25.880
It's so cute.
非常可爱。

1677
01:26:26.040 --> 01:26:29.680
It's a coming of age kind of comedy drama called Never Have I Ever.
那是一部关于成长的喜剧剧情片，叫《好想做一次》（Never Have I Ever）。

1678
01:26:30.140 --> 01:26:32.620
And the cast is wonderful and the writing is great.
演员阵容很棒，剧本也写得很好。

1679
01:26:32.780 --> 01:26:37.160
And you guys, if you watch it, you'll see Angela on it because Angela's in it in a couple of
伙计们，如果你们看了，会看到安吉拉在里面，因为安吉拉出演了

1680
01:26:37.160 --> 01:26:37.660
episodes.
几集。

1681
01:26:37.960 --> 01:26:39.200
Yes, I'm in two episodes.
是的，我演了两集。

1682
01:26:39.200 --> 01:26:40.920
I play the mom.
我演妈妈。

1683
01:26:41.180 --> 01:26:44.700
I play one of her nemesis's mom and it was really fun.
我演她其中一个死对头的妈妈，真的很有趣。

1684
01:26:44.840 --> 01:26:46.520
I'll be the mom all day long, Jenna.
我随时都可以演妈妈，珍娜。

1685
01:26:46.700 --> 01:26:47.080
I know.
我知道。

1686
01:26:48.920 --> 01:26:49.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1687
01:26:49.520 --> 01:26:54.140
Casting folks out there, if you need a mom with a little bit of sass, give me a call.
各位选角导演，如果你们需要一个带点个性的妈妈，给我打电话。

1688
01:26:54.260 --> 01:26:55.140
You know where to go.
你知道去哪儿找我。

1689
01:26:55.480 --> 01:26:57.100
Guys, thank you so much.
伙计们，非常感谢。

1690
01:26:57.200 --> 01:26:58.440
This was a really fun one.
这一期真的很有趣。

1691
01:26:58.580 --> 01:27:01.340
And we will be back next week with Branch Wars.
我们下周会回来聊《分部战争》（Branch Wars）。

1692
01:27:01.520 --> 01:27:02.040
See you then.
到时候见。

1693
01:27:02.440 --> 01:27:02.780
Bye.
再见。

